  ('luxor-egypt', '04A', 'Luxor', 'Egypt', 'Ancient Thebes', 'live', 'verified', 'desertDunes', 'Egypt & the Nile', '{"river","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Ancient Thebes - the world''s greatest open-air museum: Karnak (largest religious complex of antiquity), Luxor Temple, and across the river the Valley of the Kings (Tutankhamun), Hatshepsut''s Temple and the Colossi of Memnon","The northern gate of the Nile cruise - most Luxor<->Aswan cruises (~210 km) sail from here, stopping at Esna, Edfu and Kom Ombo","Best season Oct-Apr (Nov the sweet spot), ~25-30C; summer tops 40C - tour at dawn","US L2 Exercise Increased Caution - the Nile corridor is in the L2 zone; Do-Not-Travel areas (Sinai interior, Western Desert/Libya border) are far from Luxor; disclose L2","Sold via Egypt Nile-cruise operators + Luxor DMCs ~10-16%; site tickets non-commissionable pass-through","Currency EGP; e-Visa for most nationalities; the Grand Egyptian Museum (Cairo) opened Nov 2025 - the halo hook for the whole corridor"],"safety":{"emergency":"122 police / 123 ambulance / 126 tourist police","hospital":"Luxor International Hospital + private clinics; Cairo for major referral; carry travel-medical + evac insurance","advisory_level":"L2","activity_note":"L2 disclose - the Nile corridor is in the L2 zone (Do-Not-Travel areas are the Sinai interior and Western Desert/Libya border, far from Luxor). Main practical risk is summer heat - tour at dawn, hydrate. Use licensed balloon operators.","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to within 20km of the Egypt-Libya border, except for the town of El Salloum, where we advise against all but essential travel."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the North Sinai Governorate."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to North Sinai Governate due to continuing criminal activity and terrorist attacks on police and security forces that have resulted in deaths."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advise against all but essential travel."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern part of the South Sinai Governorate, beyond the St Catherine-Nuweibaa road, except for the coastal areas along the west and east of the peninsula."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Ismailiyah Governorate east of the Suez Canal."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the area west of the Nile Valley and Nile Delta regions, except for: Luxor, Qina, Aswan, Abu Simbel and the Valley of the Kings the Faiyum Governorate the coastal areas between the Nile Delta and Marsa Matruh the Marsa Matruh-Siwa road the oasis town of Siwa the Giza Governorate north-east of the Bahariya Oasis the White Desert and Black Desert the oasis towns of Bahariya, Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the following roads and the desert area between them and the Nile valley: the road between Giza and Farafra and within 50km either side of this road (but FCDO advises against all but essential travel on the road between Bahariya and Siwa) the road between Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the road between Kharga and Baris the road between Baris and Luxor Hala’ib Triangle and Bir Tawil Trapezoid FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Hala’ib Triangle and the Bir Tawil Trapezoid."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern part of South Sinai Governate, beyond the St Catherine-Nuweibaa road, except for the coastal areas along the west and east of the peninsula."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advise against all but essential travel due to criminal activity and terrorist attacks on police and security forces that have resulted in deaths."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the parts of the Ismailiyah Governorate which are east of the Suez Canal, due to ongoing military operations against terrorists and criminals."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the area west of the Nile Valley and Nile Delta regions due to risks from criminal activity and military operations, except for: Luxor, Qina, Valley of the Kings, Aswan and Abu Simbel the Faiyum Governorate the coastal areas between the Nile Delta and Marsa Matruh the Marsa Matruh-Siwa road the oasis town of Siwa the Giza Governorate north-east of the Bahariya Oasis the White Desert and Black Desert the oasis towns of Bahariya, Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the following roads and the desert area between them and the Nile valley: the road between Giza and Farafra and within 50km either side of this road (but FCDO advises against all but essential travel on the road between Bahariya and Siwa) the road between Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the road between Kharga and Baris the road between Baris and Luxor Tourists who enter the Western Desert areas of Bahariya Oasis, Farafra, the White Desert and Black Desert must apply for permits in advance and use an official guide."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on the road between Al Bawiti and Siwa, including the desert areas near the start of the road in Bahariya."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Hala’ib Triangle and Bir Tawil Trapezoid."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-08-04T11:10:57+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Oct-Apr (Nov the sweet spot) - comfortable ~25-30C, best light; Christmas/NY high","shoulder":"May + Sep (hotter, softer rates)","green":"Jun-Aug (40C+ - cheapest, quietest)","booking_lead":"cruises + Luxor lodges 3-9 mo for Oct-Apr + Dec holiday (limited dahabiya cabins sell out); shoulder 2-4 mo","off_season_specials":"summer heat value; pair with Aswan + Cairo/GEM","event_peaks":"Oct-Apr; Christmas/NY; N-Hemisphere autumn-winter","campaign_start":"sell Oct-Apr Nile cruises 4-6 mo out; ride the Grand Egyptian Museum (Nov 2025) halo"},"jewels":[{"name":"The Luxor to Aswan Nile cruise","si_tag":"river","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"$350-1,500+/pp; dahabiya ~$1,000-1,500/night","timing":"Oct-Apr","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Luxor↔Aswan cruise packages via Egypt DMCs + cruise lines. Commission ~10–16% DMC/operator","si":"river","blurb":"Luxor↔Aswan cruise packages via Egypt DMCs + cruise lines. Commission ~10–16% DMC/operator","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"DMC/cruise 10-16%"},{"name":"Karnak & Luxor Temple","si_tag":"culture","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"within the tour","timing":"year-round","draw_rank":1,"timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the largest religious complex of antiquity + the Nile-front temple lit at night","si":"culture","blurb":"the largest religious complex of antiquity + the Nile-front temple lit at night","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC 10-16%"},{"name":"Valley of the Kings + Hatshepsut + Colossi of Memnon","si_tag":"culture","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"within the tour","timing":"Oct-Apr","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the royal tombs incl. Tutankhamun, the terraced temple, the seated giants","si":"culture","blurb":"the royal tombs incl. Tutankhamun, the terraced temple, the seated giants","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"DMC 10-16%"},{"name":"Dawn hot-air balloon over the West Bank","si_tag":"culture","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$100-150/pp","timing":"Oct-Apr","draw_rank":3,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEAS