ate on de-escalation + consent gate"},"jewels":[{"name":"Sultan Qaboos Grand Mosque","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"one of the world''s largest mosques; giant Persian carpet and chandelier","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Muscat","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"one of the world''s largest mosques; giant Persian carpet and chandelier","when":"year-round","commission":"held - experience/DMC when the gate exists"},{"name":"Mutrah Souq","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the maze-market on the harbour, often rated the Gulf''s best","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Muscat","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"the maze-market on the harbour, often rated the Gulf''s best","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held"},{"name":"Mutrah Corniche","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"the harbour promenade with dhows","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Muscat","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"the harbour promenade with dhows","when":"year-round","commission":"held"},{"name":"Al Alam Palace + Al Jalali/Al Mirani forts","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the ceremonial palace framed by the 1580s Portuguese forts","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Muscat","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"the ceremonial palace framed by the 1580s Portuguese forts","when":"year-round","commission":"held"},{"name":"National Museum of Oman","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the national history museum opposite the palace","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Muscat","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"the national history museum opposite the palace","when":"year-round","commission":"held"},{"name":"Bait Al Zubair","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the private heritage museum in a restored house","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"web search 2026-08-10 (Viator/Tripadvisor)","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"the private heritage museum in a restored house","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held","accessed":"2026-08-10"},{"name":"Royal Opera House Muscat","si_tag":"entertainment","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"the Gulf''s landmark opera house","bookable_category":"venue (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Muscat","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"entertainment","blurb":"the Gulf''s landmark opera house","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held"},{"name":"Qurum Beach (Shatti Al Qurum)","si_tag":"entertainment","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"the palm-lined city beach","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"web search 2026-08-10 (Viator/Tripadvisor)","si":"entertainment","blurb":"the palm-lined city beach","commission":"held","accessed":"2026-08-10"},{"name":"Daymaniyat Islands","si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"the marine-reserve archipelago (~42 km offshore) for reefs, turtles and dolphins","bookable_category":"experience (held)","source":"web search 2026-08-10 (Viator/Tripadvisor)","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"the marine-reserve archipelago (~42 km offshore) for reefs, turtles and dolphins","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held - future dive/snorkel product via the gate","accessed":"2026-08-10"},{"name":"Bimmah Sinkhole","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the turquoise limestone crater ~90 min from Muscat","bookable_category":"experience (held)","source":"web search 2026-08-10 (Viator/Tripadvisor)","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"the turquoise limestone crater ~90 min from Muscat","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held","accessed":"2026-08-10"},{"name":"Wadi Shab","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"the canyon hike to emerald pools and a hidden waterfall cave","bookable_category":"experience (held)","source":"web search 2026-08-10 (Viator/Tripadvisor)","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"the canyon hike to emerald pools and a hidden waterfall cave","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held","accessed":"2026-08-10"},{"name":"Trekking Path C38 (Riyam-Mutrah)","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the old ridge trail above the harbour","bookable_category":"experience (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Muscat","si":"adventure","blurb":"the old ridge trail above the harbour","commission":"held"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the current advisory for Muscat, and can I book it through TravelWell?","a":"Oman is at U.S. State Department Level 3 - Reconsider Travel, and Muscat cannot be booked through TravelWell right now. The armed conflict that began 28 February 2026 (U.S./Israeli strikes on Iran; Iranian retaliatory strikes on all six GCC states; the Strait of Hormuz - which Oman borders - closed to commercial shipping; a State ''depart now'' order on 2 March 2026) is ongoing as of 2026-08-10. TravelWell books Level 3 only through a consent gate that is not built, so no Gulf destination is bookable regardless of level. Re-verify the level and flight picture before any travel.","source":"level+conflict supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read of the US Embassy UAE alert 4 Jun 2026 (Oman listed L3) + State-advisory press; FCDO flagged, not read in this build","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How are flights and airspace affected?","a":"Gulf airports are open but subject to short-notice closures; American Airlines cancelled Philadelphia-Doha through the end of 2026 as one regional example, and Oman sits directly on the Strait of Hormuz. Confirm every segment close to departure.","source":"supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What would a Muscat trip cover once bookable again?","a":"The Sultan Qaboos Grand Mosque, Mutrah Souq and a Corniche evening, the Royal Opera House, Al Alam Palace with the harbour forts, the National Museum and Bait Al Zubair, Qurum Beach - plus day trips to the Bimmah Sinkhole, Wadi Shab and the Daymaniyat Islands.","source":"en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Muscat (accessed 2026-08-10) + web search 2026-08-10 (Viator/Tripadvisor)","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Muscat?","a":"October-April is the mild season; summer is very hot, above 40C. Planning-only guidance while the destination is held content-only.","source":"en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Muscat (accessed 2026-08-10)","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"Is there anything specific to know about safety in the city itself?","a":"Beyond the regional conflict and the Hormuz/flight risk, Oman is generally low-crime and hospitable; the binding constraints right now are the Level 3 advisory, the flight-disruption risk, and the content-only hold. Re-verify the advisory before acting on anything here.","source":"level supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read; en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Muscat (accessed 2026-08-10)","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Muscat Travel Advisory & Guide (Oman): Level 3, Safety","meta_description":"Muscat under a U.S. Level 3 advisory amid the 2026 Gulf conflict - safety, the Hormuz/flight risk, and the sights (Grand Mosque, wadis, Daymaniyat) for when travel resumes. Held content-only.","slug":"muscat-oman","primary_keyword":"Muscat travel advisory 2026","long_tail":["Muscat Level 3 Reconsider Travel","Oman safety 2026","Sultan Qaboos Grand Mosque","Daymaniyat Islands","Wadi Shab"],"search_language":"ar (restated, not machine-translated)","local_keywords":["مسقط","جامع السلطان قابوس","سوق مطرح"],"hreflang":["en","ar"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-10"},"booking":{"bin":"content_only_L3_consent_gate_not_built","level":"L3","booking_hold":true,"codes":["L3"],"note":"HELD CONTENT-ONLY. US State Level 3 (Reconsider Travel) for Oman amid an active regional conflict that began 28 Feb 2026 (US/Israeli strikes on Iran; Iranian retaliatory strikes on all six GCC states; Strait of Hormuz - which Oman borders - closed; State depart-now for 16 countries 2 Mar 2026), ONGOING as of 2026-08-10. L3 books only via the consent gate, which Sana confirms is NOT built. FAST-MOVING: re-verify. CITATION: level+conflict supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read of the US Embassy UAE alert 4 Jun 2026 (Oman listed L3) + State-advisory press; FCDO wording for Oman NOT read in this build (required second source - verify); conflict corroborated 2026-08-10 via F1/FIA GP-cancellation coverage (Sky Sports/PlanetF1, web search)."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-10","hits":4,"misses":18,"disregarded":3,"note":"Gulf capital built content-only (safety gap); all SIs future while held; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","name":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"entertainment","name":"entertainment","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"HELD - Muscat luxury stay + Grand Mosque/Opera House + a Daymaniyat day + Wadi Shab, via the consent gate once built","why_ultra":"the ultra pull once the advisory de-escalates and the gate exists; not offered while held","earning":"n/a while held","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a while held","mor":"n/a while held","source":"TWW booking doctrine"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-10","hero":{"query":"Muscat, Oman"},"geo":{"lat":23.59,"lng":58.41}}'::jsonb, 14),
  ('red-sea-egypt', '04A', 'Red Sea', 'Egypt', '*If it''s warm-water wrecks and open-blue sharks a short', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'The Red Sea', '{"liveaboard","diveglobal","ocean","culture"}', '{}', '{"comfort","premier"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Year-round dive sea; prime windows Mar-May and Sep-Nov (liveaboard.com)","Offshore shark reefs (Brothers/Daedalus/Elphinstone) peak Jun-Nov","SS Thistlegorm + Abu Nuhas (5 wrecks) + Salem Express = dense northern wreck field","Fleet: Aggressor (x3), Emperor (x3), Master (Blue Horizon/Blue Melody), Explorer Ventures - TWW holds Aggressor + Explorer reseller lines","Advisory: State L2 (Sinai/Western-Desert L4; Red Sea dive coast outside every carve-out; FCDO concurs); chambers at Sharm/Hurghada/Marsa Shagra/Hamata (DECO 24h) - verified 2026-08-09"],"safety":{"emergency":"122 police / 123 ambulance (verify)","hospital":"coastal hospitals at Sharm el-Sheikh, Hurghada, Marsa Alam (verify)","hyperbaric":"Sharm el-Sheikh Hyperbaric Medical Center (DAN Egypt); HyperMed Hurghada (by the airport); Baro Medical Marsa Shagra (~20km N of Marsa Alam); DECO International Hamata (24h, ~135km S of Marsa Alam) - confirm itinerary chamber + dates via DAN/operator (source: emperordivers.com + deco-international.com, 2026-08-09)","advisory_level":"L2","no_fly_after_diving":"18-24h (DAN)","malaria":"none in the Red Sea resort/dive corridor (verify)","yellow_fever":"none required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to within 20km of the Egypt-Libya border, except for the town of El Salloum, where we advise against all but essential travel."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the North Sinai Governorate."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to North Sinai Governate due to continuing criminal activity and terrorist attacks on police and security forces that have resulted in deaths."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advise against all but essential travel."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern part of the South Sinai Governorate, beyond the St Catherine-Nuweibaa road, except for the coastal areas along the west and east of the peninsula."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Ismailiyah Governorate east of the Suez Canal."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the area west of the Nile Valley and Nile Delta regions, except for: Luxor, Qina, Aswan, Abu Simbel and the Valley of the Kings the Faiyum Governorate the coastal areas between the Nile Delta and Marsa Matruh the Marsa Matruh-Siwa road the oasis town of Siwa the Giza Governorate north-east of the Bahariya Oasis the White Desert and Black Desert the oasis towns of Bahariya, Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the following roads and the desert area between them and the Nile valley: the road between Giza and Farafra and within 50km either side of this road (but FCDO advises against all but essential travel on the road between Bahariya and Siwa) the road between Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the road between Kharga and Baris the road between Baris and Luxor Hala’ib Triangle and Bir Tawil Trapezoid FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Hala’ib Triangle and the Bir Tawil Trapezoid."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern part of South Sinai Governate, beyond the St Catherine-Nuweibaa road, except for the coastal areas along the west and east of the peninsula."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advise against all but essential travel due to criminal activity and terrorist attacks on police and security forces that have resulted in deaths."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the parts of the Ismailiyah Governorate which are east of the Suez Canal, due to ongoing military operations against terrorists and criminals."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the area west of the Nile Valley and Nile Delta regions due to risks from criminal activity and military operations, except for: Luxor, Qina, Valley of the Kings, Aswan and Abu Simbel the Faiyum Governorate the coastal areas between the Nile Delta and Marsa Matruh the Marsa Matruh-Siwa road the oasis town of Siwa the Giza Governorate north-east of the Bahariya Oasis the White Desert and Black Desert the oasis towns of Bahariya, Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the following roads and the desert area between them and the Nile valley: the road between Giza and Farafra and within 50km either side of this road (but FCDO advises against all but essential travel on the road between Bahariya and Siwa) the road between Farafra, Dakhla (Mut) and Kharga the road between Kharga and Baris the road between Baris and Luxor Tourists who enter the Western Desert areas of Bahariya Oasis, Farafra, the White Desert and Black Desert must apply for permits in advance and use an official guide."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on the road between Al Bawiti and Siwa, including the desert areas near the start of the road in Bahariya."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Hala’ib Triangle and Bir Tawil Trapezoid."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-08-04T11:10:57+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov (calm, warm, 30m+ viz)","shoulder":"Jun-Aug summer (30C, strongest offshore sharks, some plankton; liveaboards favour calm south)","green":"Dec-Feb (21-23C, windier offshore, fewer crowds; south stays viable)","booking_lead":"peak shark-season/marquee wreck weeks ~3-9 months for preferred vessels; shoulder nearer term; confirm per-vessel with operator","off_season_specials":"winter southern routes at lower demand; wreck routes hold year-round","event_peaks":"Jun-Nov offshore shark season is the sea''s demand spike","campaign_start":"shark-season southern routes fire Mar-Apr; wreck/shoulder fire Dec-Jan"},"jewels":[{"name":"SS Thistlegorm","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"WWII wreck, the sea''s signature dive","bookable_category":"liveaboard berth","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"WWII wreck, the sea''s signature dive","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct (Aggressor/Explorer reseller line)"},{"name":"The Brothers (Big & Small)","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"thresher and oceanic sharks, early-morning threshers","bookable_category":"liveaboard berth","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/season-calendar/best-time-to-dive-in-the-red-sea","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"thresher and oceanic sharks, early-morning threshers","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct"},{"name":"Daedalus Reef","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"hammerhead + oceanic-whitetip offshore reef, Jun-Nov","bookable_category":"liveaboard berth","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/season-calendar/best-time-to-dive-in-the-red-sea","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"hammerhead + oceanic-whitetip offshore reef, Jun-Nov","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct"},{"name":"Elphinstone Reef","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"cigar-shaped offshore reef, oceanic whitetips","bookable_category":"liveaboard berth","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"cigar-shaped offshore reef, oceanic whitetips","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct"},{"name":"Ras Mohammed (Shark & Yolanda)","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"comfort","hook":"the Sinai marine reserve","bookable_category":"liveaboard/day-boat","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"the Sinai marine reserve","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct / day-op"},{"name":"Straits of Tiran (Jackson/Woodhouse/Thomas/Gordon)","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"comfort","hook":"four northern reefs","bookable_category":"liveaboard/day-boat","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"four northern reefs","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct / day-op"},{"name":"Abu Nuhas (five wrecks)","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"comfort","hook":"the northern wreck cluster","bookable_category":"liveaboard berth","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"the northern wreck cluster","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct"},{"name":"Salem Express","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"comfort","hook":"passenger-ferry wreck (sank 1991)","bookable_category":"liveaboard berth","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"passenger-ferry wreck (sank 1991)","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct"},{"name":"Fury Shoals","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"southern reef complex from Marsa Alam","bookable_category":"liveaboard berth","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"southern reef complex from Marsa Alam","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct"},{"name":"St John''s reefs","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"290+ km2 of far-southern reef near the Sudan border","bookable_category":"liveaboard berth","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"290+ km2 of far-southern reef near the Sudan border","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct"},{"name":"Northern Wreck & Reef route","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"Thistlegorm + Abu Nuhas + Ras Mohammed + Tiran, year-round","bookable_category":"liveaboard week","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"Thistlegorm + Abu Nuhas + Ras Mohammed + Tiran, year-round","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct (Aggressor/Explorer)"},{"name":"Southern BDE offshore shark route","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"Brothers-Daedalus-Elphinstone, Jun-Nov","bookable_category":"liveaboard week","source":"https://www.liveaboard.com/diving/season-calendar/best-time-to-dive-in-the-red-sea","timing":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"Brothers-Daedalus-Elphinstone, Jun-Nov","when":"Mar-May & Sep-Nov","commission":"fleet-direct (Aggressor/Explorer)"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the current advisory for the Egyptian Red Sea, and how do I dive it responsibly?","a":"The U.S. State Department places Egypt at Level 2 - Exercise Increased Caution (accessed 2026-08-09). The Northern and Middle Sinai Peninsula and parts of the Western Desert carry a Level 4 (Do Not Travel) carve-out; the Red Sea coast sits outside every carve-out, so Hurghada and the northern Red Sea coast carry no sub-zone restriction. The UK FCDO draws the same interior zones in its own words and names no Red Sea resort; the stricter baseline (State Level 2) sets the posture. Carry DAN membership plus separate dive-accident insurance and observe an 18-24 hour no-fly window after diving.","source":"travel.state.gov/en/international-travel/travel-advisories/egypt.html + gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt/warnings-and-insurance (both accessed 2026-08-09)","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is there a recompression chamber, and how remote is care?","a":"The Red Sea coast runs a dense chamber network. Northern routes are covered by the Hyperbaric Medical Center in Sharm el-Sheikh (DAN Egypt) and HyperMed in Hurghada (next to the airport); southern routes by Baro Medical in Marsa Shagra (about 20 km north of Marsa Alam) and the DECO International chamber in Hamata (a 24-hour recompression and medical-emergency facility about 135 km south of Marsa Alam). Confirm the chamber covering your itinerary and its readiness on your dates via the operator or DAN. Offshore reefs are hours from port, so insurance and a conservative profile matter most there.","source":"emperordivers.com/recompression-dcs-and-diving-safety + deco-international.com (accessed 2026-08-09)","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive the Red Sea?","a":"March-May and September-November are the optimal windows - calm seas, warm water and 30 m+ visibility. Summer (June-August) pushes water to 30C with strong offshore shark action but occasional plankton; winter (December-February) drops to 21-23C and can be windy offshore.","source":"liveaboard.com/diving/season-calendar/best-time-to-dive-in-the-red-sea","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"When can I see oceanic whitetips, hammerheads and threshers?","a":"June-November is the offshore shark window: oceanic whitetips, grey reef and scalloped hammerheads around Daedalus and Elphinstone, with The Brothers known for thresher sharks in the early morning.","source":"liveaboard.com/diving/season-calendar/best-time-to-dive-in-the-red-sea","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"North route or south route - which liveaboard week?","a":"North runs the wrecks and reefs - SS Thistlegorm, Abu Nuhas, Ras Mohammed and the Straits of Tiran (Jackson, Woodhouse, Thomas, Gordon). South runs the offshore shark reefs (Brothers, Daedalus, Elphinstone) and the remote Fury Shoals and St John''s near the Sudan border; liveaboards favour the calm southern conditions in summer.","source":"liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"What certification and conditions should I plan for?","a":"The offshore reefs (Brothers, Daedalus, Elphinstone) are current-swept blue-water sites suited to experienced divers; the northern wrecks and Tiran reefs suit a wider range with a guide. Nitrox is standard on most liveaboards for the repetitive multi-day profile. Dive within your certification and the operator briefing.","source":"liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How far ahead do Red Sea liveaboards book?","a":"Peak shark-season southern weeks (June-November) and the marquee wreck routes fill earliest; hold a berth roughly 3-9 months out for peak windows and preferred vessels, with shoulder weeks bookable nearer term. Confirm current per-vessel lead times with the operator.","source":"liveaboard.com/diving/egypt","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Red Sea Liveaboard Diving, Egypt: Wrecks, Sharks & Season","meta_description":"The Egyptian Red Sea liveaboard sea - SS Thistlegorm and the northern wrecks, the Brothers-Daedalus-Elphinstone shark reefs, season, operators and safety.","slug":"red-sea-egypt","primary_keyword":"Red Sea liveaboard diving","long_tail":["SS Thistlegorm wreck dive","Brothers Daedalus Elphinstone sharks","Red Sea dive season","Egypt liveaboard operators","Ras Mohammed Straits of Tiran"],"search_language":"ar-EG (restated, not machine-translated)","local_keywords":["غوص البحر الأحمر","حطام ثيسلغورم","غطس الإخوة دايدلوس"],"hreflang":["en","ar-EG"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-09"},"booking":{"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","level":"L2 (Exercise Increased Caution)","codes":["L2"],"note":"US State Dept Level 2, accessed 2026-08-09 (travel.state.gov/en/.../egypt.html). Level 4 (Do Not Travel) carve-outs: Northern and Middle Sinai Peninsula + parts of the Western Desert. The Red Sea dive coast (Hurghada/Marsa Alam/southern Sinai resort strip) sits outside every carve-out. FCDO cross-check (gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/egypt, accessed 2026-08-09): advises against all travel to North Sinai Governorate, all but essential to parts of South Sinai + Western Desert + within 20km of the Libya border; names no Red Sea resort. Both agree the dive coast is unrestricted; stricter baseline (State L2) drives posture."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-09","hits":4,"misses":18,"disregarded":3,"note":"Liveaboard-diving destination; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"liveaboard","name":"liveaboard","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","name":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","name":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private full-boat liveaboard charter (Aggressor/Master/Emperor) + Cairo-Nile add-on","why_ultra":"the Red Sea ultra pull is a private charter of a premium vessel for a family/club, paired with a Nile land week","earning":"held fleet reseller line for Aggressor/Explorer; verify Master/Emperor charter terms","virtuoso_value_add":"verify - not documented","mor":"commission-on-net where the fleet pays; no net-rate resale markup","source":"handoff/LIVEABOARD-OPERATOR-GRID-2026-08-09.md"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-09","hero":{"query":"Red Sea, Egypt"},"geo":{"lat":25.5,"lng":34.8}}'::jsonb, 15),
  ('riyadh-saudi-arabia', '04A', 'Riyadh', 'Saudi Arabia', '*When the Gulf reopens, the capital of Diriyah and', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'The Gulf', '{"culture","entertainment","adventure","family"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["HELD CONTENT-ONLY: US State L3 Reconsider Travel (Saudi Arabia) amid the ongoing 28 Feb 2026 Gulf conflict; L3 consent gate NOT built - not bookable","CARVE-OUTS FLAGGED NOT READ: Saudi historically names stricter Yemen-border + Eastern-Province (Qatif) zones - verify at travel.state.gov","Marquee sights (planning only): Diriyah/At-Turaif UNESCO, National Museum, Masmak, Kingdom Centre Sky Bridge, Edge of the World","Event flag: 2026 Bahrain + Saudi F1 GPs CANCELLED (F1/FIA 15 Mar 2026) over the conflict","Advisory + conflict supplied by Strategy Claude (2026-08-09 read); FCDO Saudi wording NOT read (verify); RE-VERIFY before travel"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 police / 997 ambulance (verify)","hospital":"major hospitals in Riyadh (verify)","hyperbaric":"not applicable (not a dive destination)","advisory_level":"L3","regional_conflict":"Armed conflict began 28 Feb 2026 (US/Israeli strikes on Iran; Iranian retaliatory strikes on all six GCC states; Hormuz closed; State depart-now 2 Mar 2026); ongoing as of 2026-08-10","no_fly_after_diving":"n/a","malaria":"none in Riyadh (verify)","yellow_fever":"only if arriving from an endemic country","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia","read":"2026-08-20","page_updated":"2026-07-25T18:34:42+01:00","alert_status":["avoid_all_travel_to_parts","avoid_all_but_essential_travel_to_parts"],"basis":"exact","note":"CORRECTED CC Job 100, 2026-08-20. This row read posture 1 - \"the FCDO names no advisory against travel anywhere in this country\" - while the FCDO advises against all travel to within 10km of the Yemen border and all but essential travel to areas beyond it. The earlier rule parsed prose only, and the FCDO writes this restriction as a bulleted list, so the phrase regex never matched. Posture now comes from their own `alert_status` field first. ⛔ WHETHER THIS DESTINATION SITS INSIDE A NAMED AREA IS A JUDGEMENT AND IS A PERSON''S."}},"timing":{"peak":"Oct-Apr (cool season; Riyadh Season) - planning only","shoulder":"Apr & Oct edges","green":"May-Sep (45C+ desert heat)","booking_lead":"N/A while held content-only (L3, consent gate not built)","off_season_specials":"n/a while held","event_peaks":"Riyadh Season Oct-Apr (Boulevard World)","campaign_start":"none while held; re-evaluate on de-escalation + consent gate"},"jewels":[{"name":"Diriyah / At-Turaif (UNESCO)","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"the mud-brick birthplace of the Saudi state","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"the mud-brick birthplace of the Saudi state","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held - experience/DMC when the gate exists"},{"name":"Bujairi Terrace (Diriyah)","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"the dining terrace overlooking At-Turaif","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"web search 2026-08-10 (Thrillophilia/Tripadvisor)","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"the dining terrace overlooking At-Turaif","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held","accessed":"2026-08-10"},{"name":"National Museum (King Abdulaziz Historical Centre)","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"the national history museum and its historical centre","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"the national history museum and its historical centre","when":"year-round","commission":"held"},{"name":"Masmak Fortress","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the 1902 mud-brick fort and museum","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"the 1902 mud-brick fort and museum","when":"year-round","commission":"held"},{"name":"Murabba Palace","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"King Abdulaziz''s palace, now a museum","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"King Abdulaziz''s palace, now a museum","when":"year-round","commission":"held"},{"name":"Souq al-Thumairi (Deira)","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the old antique-and-carpet souq","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"the old antique-and-carpet souq","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held"},{"name":"Kingdom Centre Sky Bridge","si_tag":"entertainment","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the 99th-floor skybridge over the city","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"entertainment","blurb":"the 99th-floor skybridge over the city","when":"year-round","commission":"held"},{"name":"Riyadh Season / Boulevard World","si_tag":"entertainment","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the Oct-Apr entertainment season","bookable_category":"event (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"entertainment","blurb":"the Oct-Apr entertainment season","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held"},{"name":"Salam Park","si_tag":"family","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"the city''s family lake-park","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"web search 2026-08-10 (Thrillophilia/Tripadvisor)","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"family","blurb":"the city''s family lake-park","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held","accessed":"2026-08-10"},{"name":"Edge of the World (Jebel Fihrayn)","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"the escarpment cliffs on the desert edge outside Riyadh","bookable_category":"experience (held)","source":"web search 2026-08-10 (Thrillophilia/Tripadvisor)","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"the escarpment cliffs on the desert edge outside Riyadh","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held - DMC/tour when the gate exists","accessed":"2026-08-10"},{"name":"Wadi Hanifah","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"the rehabilitated 80-km desert-valley park","bookable_category":"attraction (held)","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"the rehabilitated 80-km desert-valley park","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held"},{"name":"Desert day trip from Riyadh","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"dune and escarpment excursions","bookable_category":"experience (held)","source":"web search 2026-08-10 (Thrillophilia/Tripadvisor)","timing":"Oct-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"dune and escarpment excursions","when":"Oct-Apr","commission":"held","accessed":"2026-08-10"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the current advisory for Riyadh, and can I book it through TravelWell?","a":"Saudi Arabia is at U.S. State Department Level 3 - Reconsider Travel, and Riyadh cannot be booked through TravelWell right now. The armed conflict that began 28 February 2026 (U.S./Israeli strikes on Iran; Iranian retaliatory strikes on all six GCC states; the Strait of Hormuz closed; a State ''depart now'' order on 2 March 2026) is ongoing as of 2026-08-10. TravelWell books Level 3 only through a consent gate that is not built, so no Gulf destination is bookable regardless of level. Saudi Arabia''s advisory has historically carried stricter sub-national carve-outs (near the Yemen border and in parts of the Eastern Province) - verify those against the live advisory. Re-verify everything before any travel.","source":"level+conflict supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read of the US Embassy UAE alert 4 Jun 2026 (Saudi listed L3) + State-advisory press; carve-outs + FCDO flagged, not read in this build","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How are flights and airspace affected?","a":"Gulf airports are open but subject to short-notice closures; American Airlines cancelled Philadelphia-Doha through the end of 2026 as one regional example. Confirm every segment close to departure.","source":"supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What would a Riyadh trip cover once bookable again?","a":"Diriyah and At-Turaif (UNESCO) with the Bujairi Terrace, the National Museum at the King Abdulaziz Historical Centre, Masmak Fortress and the old Deira souq, Kingdom Centre''s Sky Bridge, Wadi Hanifah, Salam Park, and a day trip to the Edge of the World cliffs. Riyadh Season (Oct-Apr) is the marquee event window.","source":"en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh (accessed 2026-08-10) + web search 2026-08-10 (Edge of the World/Bujairi/Salam Park)","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Riyadh?","a":"October-April is the cool season (and Riyadh Season); summer is extreme desert heat, above 45C. Planning-only guidance while the destination is held content-only.","source":"en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh (accessed 2026-08-10)","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"Is there anything specific to know about safety and local law?","a":"Beyond the regional conflict and the flight disruption, Saudi Arabia enforces conservative local laws and dress codes; the binding constraints right now are the Level 3 advisory, the sub-national carve-outs to verify, and the content-only hold. Re-verify the advisory before acting on anything here.","source":"level supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read; en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Riyadh (accessed 2026-08-10)","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Riyadh Travel Advisory & Guide (Saudi Arabia): Level 3","meta_description":"Riyadh under a U.S. Level 3 advisory amid the 2026 Gulf conflict - safety, the carve-outs to verify, and the sights (Diriyah, Edge of the World) for when travel resumes. Held content-only.","slug":"riyadh-saudi-arabia","primary_keyword":"Riyadh travel advisory 2026","long_tail":["Riyadh Level 3 Reconsider Travel","Saudi Arabia safety 2026","Diriyah At-Turaif","Edge of the World Riyadh","Riyadh Season"],"search_language":"ar (restated, not machine-translated)","local_keywords":["الرياض","الدرعية","حافة العالم"],"hreflang":["en","ar"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-10"},"booking":{"bin":"content_only_L3_consent_gate_not_built","level":"L3","booking_hold":true,"codes":["L3"],"note":"HELD CONTENT-ONLY. US State Level 3 (Reconsider Travel) for Saudi Arabia amid an active regional conflict that began 28 Feb 2026 (US/Israeli strikes on Iran; Iranian retaliatory strikes on all six GCC states; Hormuz closed; State depart-now for 16 countries 2 Mar 2026), ONGOING as of 2026-08-10. L3 books only via the consent gate, which Sana confirms is NOT built. CARVE-OUTS FLAGGED, NOT READ: Saudi historically names stricter zones near the Yemen border + parts of the Eastern Province (Qatif) - verify current levels at travel.state.gov. FAST-MOVING: re-verify. CITATION: level+conflict supplied by Strategy Claude from a 2026-08-09 read of the US Embassy UAE alert 4 Jun 2026 (Saudi listed L3) + State-advisory press; FCDO wording for Saudi NOT read in this build (required second source - verify); conflict corroborated 2026-08-10 via F1/FIA GP-cancellation coverage (Sky Sports/PlanetF1, web search)."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-10","hits":4,"misses":18,"disregarded":3,"note":"Gulf capital built content-only (safety gap); all SIs future while held; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"entertainment","name":"entertainment","status":"future"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"future"},{"si":"family","name":"family","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"HELD - Diriyah luxury stay + At-Turaif + Edge of the World desert day, via the consent gate once built","why_ultra":"the ultra pull once the advisory de-escalates and the gate exists; not offered while held","earning":"n/a while held","virtuoso_value_add":"n/a while held","mor":"n/a while held","source":"TWW booking doctrine"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-10","hero":{"query":"Riyadh, Saudi Arabia"},"geo":{"lat":24.71,"lng":46.68}}'::jsonb, 16),
