na River as far as the town of Saka within 15km of the east coast between the Tana River and the Galana (Athi-Galana-Sabaki) River Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to: Garissa Town Tana River County north of the Tana River as far as the town of Saka within 15km of the east coast between the Tana River and the Galana (Athi-Galana-Sabaki) River There have been frequent attacks in the north-eastern border regions, most of which were attributed to Al Shabaab."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-06-24T12:48:44+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Oct (dry, clearest Kilimanjaro, wildlife at the marshes) + Jan-Feb (dry, clear mountain)","shoulder":"Nov + Mar (quieter, softer rates)","green":"Apr-May (long rains - lush, quiet, cheapest; mountain often clouded)","booking_lead":"lodges + Kenya-circuit 4-9 mo for Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb (under-Kili luxury sells out); shoulder 2-4 mo; green 1-2 mo","off_season_specials":"Apr-May green-season value; combine Maasai Mara / Tsavo / Laikipia (rhino)","event_peaks":"Jun-Oct + Christmas/NY + Easter; N-Hemisphere summer","campaign_start":"Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb clear-mountain safaris 6-9 mo out; green value by prior Nov-Dec; bundle Amboseli + Laikipia (rhino) to complete the Big Five"},"jewels":[{"name":"Elephants under Kilimanjaro (Super Tuskers)","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~$400-2,000/pp/day","timing":"Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb; dawn","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the most iconic image in safari — great herds and giant-tusked bulls crossing the dust with the snow-capped 5,896-m peak behind","si":"safari","blurb":"the most iconic image in safari — great herds and giant-tusked bulls crossing the dust with the snow-capped 5,896-m peak behind","when":"Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb; dawn","commission":"safari DMC 10-16%"},{"name":"Observation Hill + the swamp game","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"within the safari","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"climb the park''s one hill for the panorama of the snowmelt swamps, then game-drive the marsh edges where elephant, buffalo","si":"safari","blurb":"climb the park''s one hill for the panorama of the snowmelt swamps, then game-drive the marsh edges where elephant, buffalo","when":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","commission":"safari DMC 10-16%"},{"name":"Dawn hot-air balloon over Amboseli","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$400-500/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"sunrise over the elephant plains with Kilimanjaro on the horizon, then a bush breakfast — the signature aerial view","si":"adventure","blurb":"sunrise over the elephant plains with Kilimanjaro on the horizon, then a bush breakfast — the signature aerial view","when":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","commission":"DMC/camp 10-15%"},{"name":"The Amboseli Elephant Research Project","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the longest wild-elephant study on Earth — 3,500+ named individuals, matriarchal society; behind-the-scenes conservation-tourism visits with the Trust","si":"deepdive","blurb":"the longest wild-elephant study on Earth — 3,500+ named individuals, matriarchal society; behind-the-scenes conservation-tourism visits with the Trust","when":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","commission":"conservation/DMC"},{"name":"A luxury-lodge honeymoon under Kilimanjaro","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$700-2,000+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 4-9 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Tortilis, ol Donyo and Angama Amboseli frame the mountain from private decks and plunge pools — sundowners, bush dinners and the elephants below; honeymoon-grade","si":"ultra","blurb":"Tortilis, ol Donyo and Angama Amboseli frame the mountain from private decks and plunge pools — sundowners, bush dinners and the elephants below; honeymoon-grade","when":"standing; peak 4-9 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC"},{"name":"A Kilimanjaro-view honeymoon lodge","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Tortilis, ol Donyo and Angama Amboseli frame the mountain from private decks and plunge pools — sundowners, bush dinners and the elephants below; honeymoon-grade","si":"romance","blurb":"Tortilis, ol Donyo and Angama Amboseli frame the mountain from private decks and plunge pools — sundowners, bush dinners and the elephants below; honeymoon-grade","when":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","commission":"consortia/host"},{"name":"A Maasai village visit","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$20-50/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the Maasai who share the Amboseli ecosystem — a boma visit, dance and beadwork with a fair-trade operator","si":"culture","blurb":"the Maasai who share the Amboseli ecosystem — a boma visit, dance and beadwork with a fair-trade operator","when":"Jun-Oct  + Jan-Feb","commission":"DMC/community"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Amboseli?","a":"Elephants and remoteness. Amboseli''s herds are large and free-ranging - keep a respectful distance, stay in the vehicle and follow your guide (elephants can charge if threatened). Malaria is the main health risk (prophylaxis + DEET), and the park is remote - carry AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30 days) + travel-medical insurance.","source":"kws.go.ke","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Amboseli - for game and Kilimanjaro?","a":"Jun-Oct and Jan-Feb (dry) - wildlife concentrates at the marshes and the mountain is clearest; go on a game drive at first light, before the summit hides behind cloud by ~10am. The green season is lush and better value.","source":"safaribookings.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Will I actually see Kilimanjaro and Super Tuskers?","a":"Often, but not guaranteed - the peak is cloud-shy, so plan multiple dawn drives for the clear-mountain shot. Amboseli is also one of the last strongholds of giant-tusked bulls; a good guide and a couple of days maximise both.","source":"privatetourscapetown.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Is there rhino at Amboseli?","a":"No - rhino were hunted to local extinction here in the 1970s, so Amboseli is a four-of-the-Big-Five park (elephant, lion, buffalo, leopard). For rhino, pair it with Ol Pejeta/Lewa in Laikipia.","source":"delfintours.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Kenya?","a":"An eTA (Kenya replaced visas with the eTA in 2024 - apply at least 2 weeks ahead). Yellow fever is compulsory only if you arrive from a YF-risk country; CDC recommends the vaccine for most.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safari"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Amboseli Safari Guide: Elephants Under Kilimanjaro, Super Tuskers, Best Time & Fees","meta_description":"Plan an Amboseli safari - elephants under Kilimanjaro, some of the last Super Tuskers, the iconic mountain view (clearest at dawn Jun-Oct + Jan-Feb), four of the Big Five, the 1972 elephant-research legacy, 2026 fees and cost, with real safety, timing and evac intel.","slug":"amboseli-kenya","primary_keyword":"Amboseli safari","long_tail":["Amboseli elephants Kilimanjaro","Amboseli Super Tuskers","best time to visit Amboseli","Amboseli park fees 2026","Amboseli vs Maasai Mara","is Amboseli safe","Amboseli balloon safari"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Amboseli","Kilimanjaro","tembo","Wamaasai","Kilima cha theluji","safari ya puto"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-31"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":["exercise-increased-caution","crime","urban-unrest"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Kenya US L2 Exercise Increased Caution - elevated risk in Nairobi/urban areas, not Amboseli; safe licensed-operator safari. Disclose L2. Re-verify each cycle."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; SAFARI is the launch/demo SI - primary safari not globaladv; balloon/Kilimanjaro-photography = globaladv; elephant-research legacy = deepdive; NO rhino here; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"elephants + Super Tuskers; 4 of Big Five (no rhino)"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"balloon + Kilimanjaro photography + Observation Hill"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"Amboseli Elephant Research Project (1972)"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future","note":"Maasai"}],"ultra":[{"name":"ol Donyo Lodge (Great Plains, Chyulu Hills) - the apex Kili view","why_ultra":"starbeds + plunge-pool suites with Kilimanjaro across the plains, horse-riding + walking on a private wilderness","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,500-2,800+/night"},{"name":"A private Amboseli + elephant-research day + balloon","why_ultra":"exclusive-vehicle safari + a behind-the-scenes elephant-research visit + the dawn balloon","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"A Big-Five-completing week (Amboseli + Laikipia + Mara)","why_ultra":"elephants-and-Kili + rhino in Laikipia + the migration in the Mara, private-guided throughout","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-31","hero":{"query":"Amboseli National Park, Kenya"},"geo":{"lat":-2.65,"lng":37.26}}'::jsonb, 4),
  ('bwindi-impenetrable-uganda', '05A', 'Bwindi Impenetrable National Park', 'Uganda', 'Half the world''s mountain gorillas', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Uganda — Bwindi / SW gorilla country', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","deepdive","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["BOOKING HOLD: Uganda US L4 Do Not Travel driven by an Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. CONTENT-ONLY, no Book path, no waiver. DYNAMIC - re-verify each cycle, flip to live when it clears. Redirect gorilla demand to Rwanda Volcanoes","The world''s premier gorilla forest (UNESCO 1994): ~459 mountain gorillas - nearly HALF the world''s - across ~25 habituated groups (9 for trekking) in an ancient Afromontane rainforest","Permit $800 (foreign non-resident; $600 low-season Apr/May/Nov), operator-only since 1 Mar 2026; the Uganda-ONLY 4-hour Gorilla Habituation Experience (Rushaga) $1,500 -> $1,800 on 1 Jan 2027","One of Earth''s most biodiverse forests: 200+ trees, 350+ birds (Albertine Rift endemics), 202 butterflies; the Batwa first people","Yellow fever MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe); eVisa (no visa-on-arrival); malaria in all regions incl. Bwindi (prophylaxis); strenuous steep/muddy trek (sectors Buhoma easiest, Nkuringo hardest)","Live twin = volcanoes-np-rwanda (Rwanda, bookable). Trek rules when reopened: 7-10m distance, mandatory mask, max 1hr, max 8/group, armed ranger, min age 15, no trekking if ill"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 / 112","hospital":"Remote - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Kihihi/Kampala","malaria":"present in all regions incl. Bwindi lowland forest - prophylaxis","yellow_fever":"MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe, >=10 days before)","ebola":"Sudan virus outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. Health information, not an advisory against travel - the FCDO restricts nothing in Uganda; re-verify current outbreak status before travel","activity_note":"Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak is standing health information to re-verify each cycle - not a booking hold (health-based holds released, David 2026-08-29). Trek rules 7-10m/mask/1hr/max8/armed ranger/no-trek-if-ill; YF mandatory; strenuous high-forest hike","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the DRC provinces that border Uganda."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to these DRC provinces."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the provinces of DRC that border Uganda, including Virunga National Park."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to South Sudan."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-27T15:00:28+01:00"}},"timing":{"booking_status":"HELD - no live demand capture while Level 4 stands (no campaigns/fire-dates)","latent_peak":"Jun-Aug/Sep + Dec-Feb (drier, firmer trails; permits scarce) - IF cleared","latent_green":"Apr/May + Nov (rains, muddier; $600 low-season permit)","latent_booking_lead":"permits + lodges 3-6 mo - NOT applicable while held","reverify_trigger":"check Uganda''s advisory EVERY publish cycle - DYNAMIC health advisory; flip Bwindi to live the moment it drops below L4","redirect":"live gorilla demand -> volcanoes-np-rwanda (Rwanda, bookable, US L3, ~2h from Kigali)"},"jewels":[{"name":"The mountain-gorilla trek","si_tag":"safari","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path ($800 permit latent)","timing":"HELD; latent Jun-Aug + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":null,"hook":"nearly half the world''s mountain gorillas in an ancient UNESCO forest — a one-hour habituated-family encounter on a $800 permit. STATUS: HELD","si":"safari","blurb":"nearly half the world''s mountain gorillas in an ancient UNESCO forest — a one-hour habituated-family encounter on a $800 permit. STATUS: HELD","when":"HELD; latent Jun-Aug + Dec-Feb","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"The 4-hour Gorilla Habituation Experience","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"held","tier":"ultra","price_band":"HELD ($1,500 -> $1,800 2027 latent)","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"Uganda-only — four hours with a semi-habituated family and the researchers, in the Rushaga sector. STATUS: HELD","si":"adventure","blurb":"Uganda-only — four hours with a semi-habituated family and the researchers, in the Rushaga sector. STATUS: HELD","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"The biodiversity of an ancient forest","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"one of Earth''s most biodiverse Afromontane rainforests — 200+ trees, 350+ birds, 202 butterflies. STATUS: HELD","si":"deepdive","blurb":"one of Earth''s most biodiverse Afromontane rainforests — 200+ trees, 350+ birds, 202 butterflies. STATUS: HELD","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"The Batwa cultural experience","si_tag":"culture","status":"held","tier":"essential","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"the forest''s first people — a moving visit to Batwa communities on the forest edge, their music, hunting heritage and displacement story. STATUS: HELD","si":"culture","blurb":"the forest''s first people — a moving visit to Batwa communities on the forest edge, their music, hunting heritage and displacement story. STATUS: HELD","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"A forest-lodge gorilla honeymoon (held)","si_tag":"ultra","status":"held","tier":"luxury","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"Bwindi Lodge, Sanctuary Gorilla Forest Camp, Clouds Mountain Gorilla Lodge — fireside forest luxury after the trek","si":"ultra","blurb":"Bwindi Lodge, Sanctuary Gorilla Forest Camp, Clouds Mountain Gorilla Lodge — fireside forest luxury after the trek","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Where can I trek gorillas instead, right now?","a":"Rwanda - Volcanoes National Park. **FCDO travel advice for Uganda:** the FCDO names no advisory against travel to Uganda. *https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda — page updated 2026-07-27.*","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Will this clear - should I wait for Bwindi?","a":"Possibly - this is a health-driven, dynamic advisory (an outbreak, not conflict), so it can be lifted when the outbreak is contained. We re-verify Uganda''s status every publish cycle and will flip Bwindi to bookable the moment it drops below Level 4. For a firm 2026 trip, book Rwanda now.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What would Bwindi offer when it reopens?","a":"The world''s premier gorilla forest - nearly half the planet''s mountain gorillas, the $800 permit (cheaper than Rwanda), the Uganda-only 4-hour Habituation Experience, exceptional biodiversity and the Batwa culture. All held until the advisory lifts.","source":"whc.unesco.org","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When it reopens, how hard is the Bwindi trek and what are the rules?","a":"Moderate-to-strenuous - 1-6 hours through steep, muddy forest (sectors from easy Buhoma to hard Nkuringo); then max 1 hour, 7-10m distance, a mandatory face mask, max 8 per group, an armed ranger, and no trekking if ill (gorillas are highly susceptible to human disease).","source":"kabiza.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"What are the non-Ebola health requirements for Uganda?","a":"Yellow fever is mandatory for entry (all travelers >=1 yr, checked at Entebbe, vaccinate >=10 days before); malaria prophylaxis is essential (all regions incl. Bwindi); carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance. All moot while the L4 hold stands.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Bwindi Gorilla Trekking, Uganda: Half the World''s Mountain Gorillas - On Hold (Level 4 / Ebola)","meta_description":"Bwindi Impenetrable Forest - nearly half the world''s mountain gorillas, the $800 permit and the Uganda-only 4-hour Habituation Experience - is currently a US Level 4 ''Do Not Travel'' zone (Ebola outbreak). What it is, why it''s held, and where to trek gorillas instead (Rwanda''s Volcanoes NP).","slug":"bwindi-impenetrable-uganda","primary_keyword":"Bwindi gorilla trekking","long_tail":["Bwindi mountain gorillas","Uganda gorilla permit $800","gorilla habituation experience Uganda","is Uganda safe Ebola","Bwindi vs Volcanoes Rwanda","Bwindi UNESCO"],"search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Bwindi","empologoma z''ensozi","Rushaga","Buhoma","Batwa","UNESCO"],"hreflang":["en"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-01"},"booking":{"bin":"booking_hold","level":"L4","codes":["do-not-travel","ebola-sudan-virus-pheic","health-outbreak"],"book_suppressed":true,"waiver":false,"dynamic":true,"note":"Uganda US L4 Do Not Travel driven by an Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. CONTENT-ONLY, Book button suppressed, no waiver. DYNAMIC health advisory - re-verify EVERY publish cycle; flip to live the moment it drops below L4. Redirect live gorilla demand to volcanoes-np-rwanda (Rwanda, bookable)."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; EVERY hit is HELD behind the L4 booking hold - no SI is servable while Level 4 stands; safari = the gorilla trek (primary when live), globaladv = the Habituation Experience; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"held","note":"mountain gorilla trek"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"held","note":"the 4-hour Gorilla Habituation Experience (Uganda-only)"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"held"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"held","note":"UNESCO biodiversity"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"held","note":"the Batwa"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Clouds Mountain Gorilla Lodge / Bwindi Lodge (HELD)","why_ultra":"the forest''s apex stays - barefoot-luxury on the Nkuringo/Buhoma edge; documented for the day the hold lifts, sold by no one today","earning":"none while held","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"n/a (L4 booking hold)","tier":"ultra","status":"HELD"},{"name":"A private double-permit + Habituation week (HELD)","why_ultra":"the standard trek + the Uganda-only 4-hour habituation + biodiversity + Batwa, privately guided - latent","earning":"none while held","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"n/a (L4 booking hold)","tier":"ultra","status":"HELD"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Bwindi Impenetrable National Park, Uganda"},"geo":{"lat":-1.05,"lng":29.65}}'::jsonb, 5),
  ('kibale-forest-uganda', '05A', 'Kibale Forest National Park', 'Uganda', 'The primate capital of the world', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Uganda — Kibale Forest', '{"adventure","deepdive","ultra","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["BOOKING HOLD: Uganda US L4 Do Not Travel driven by an Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. CONTENT-ONLY, no Book path, no waiver. DYNAMIC - re-verify each cycle, flip to live when it clears. Redirect chimp demand to Rwanda''s Nyungwe","The primate capital of the world: up to ~1,500 chimpanzees and 13 primate species in a lush tropical rainforest - the richest primate community in East Africa","The chimp trek is the draw (globaladv-primary) - $250 permit (foreign non-resident), plus the full-day Habituation Experience ~$300; safari (big game) is a documented MISS - a forest, not a savanna","Bigodi wetland (Magombe) community birding walk on the forest edge (200+ birds + primates) - a model of community tourism","Yellow fever MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe); eVisa (no visa-on-arrival); malaria in all regions incl. Kibale forest (prophylaxis); chimp-trek rules ~8m/mask/1hr/ranger/no-trek-if-ill","Live twin = nyungwe-forest-rwanda (Rwanda, bookable, US L3 - same chimp trek). Anchors the Uganda cluster with bwindi/queen-elizabeth/murchison-falls"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 / 112","hospital":"Remote - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Fort Portal/Kampala","malaria":"present in all regions incl. Kibale forest - prophylaxis","yellow_fever":"MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe, >=10 days before)","ebola":"Sudan virus outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. Health information, not an advisory against travel - the FCDO restricts nothing in Uganda; re-verify current outbreak status before travel","activity_note":"Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak is standing health information to re-verify each cycle - not a booking hold (health-based holds released, David 2026-08-29). Chimp-trek rules ~8m/mask/1hr/ranger/no-trek-if-ill; warm humid forest walk (moderate)","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the DRC provinces that border Uganda."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to these DRC provinces."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the provinces of DRC that border Uganda, including Virunga National Park."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to South Sudan."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-27T15:00:28+01:00"}},"timing":{"booking_status":"HELD - no live demand capture while Level 4 stands (no campaigns/fire-dates)","latent_peak":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb (drier, firmer forest trails; permits scarce) - IF cleared","latent_green":"Mar-May + Oct-Nov (rains, muddier; chimps lower/closer with fruiting)","latent_booking_lead":"permits + lodges 2-4 mo peak - NOT applicable while held","reverify_trigger":"check Uganda''s advisory EVERY publish cycle - DYNAMIC health advisory; flip to live the moment it drops below L4","redirect":"live chimp-trek demand -> nyungwe-forest-rwanda (Rwanda, bookable, US L3 - the direct live twin)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Chimpanzee trekking in the primate capital","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD ($250 permit latent)","timing":"HELD; latent Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":null,"hook":"the finest chimp trek in Africa — up to 1,500 chimps in a lush rainforest","si":"adventure","blurb":"the finest chimp trek in Africa — up to 1,500 chimps in a lush rainforest","when":"HELD; latent Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"The full-day Chimpanzee Habituation Experience","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD (~$300 latent)","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"shadow the researchers from dawn nest to dusk nest with a semi-habituated community","si":"adventure","blurb":"shadow the researchers from dawn nest to dusk nest with a semi-habituated community","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"13 primates + a birding forest","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"the richest primate community in East Africa — 13 species plus 370+ birds; a specialist primate/birding week. STATUS: HELD","si":"deepdive","blurb":"the richest primate community in East Africa — 13 species plus 370+ birds; a specialist primate/birding week. STATUS: HELD","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"The Bigodi wetland community walk","si_tag":"culture","status":"held","tier":"essential","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"the community-run Bigodi Swamp walk on the forest edge — 200+ birds, more primates and a model of community tourism. STATUS: HELD","si":"culture","blurb":"the community-run Bigodi Swamp walk on the forest edge — 200+ birds, more primates and a model of community tourism. STATUS: HELD","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"A crater-and-forest lodge honeymoon (held)","si_tag":"ultra","status":"held","tier":"comfort","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"Kyaninga Lodge above its crater lake, Ndali Lodge, Primate Lodge in the forest — the ultra way to do the chimps","si":"ultra","blurb":"Kyaninga Lodge above its crater lake, Ndali Lodge, Primate Lodge in the forest — the ultra way to do the chimps","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Where can I trek chimps instead, right now?","a":"Rwanda - Nyungwe Forest. We route all chimp demand there. **FCDO travel advice for Uganda:** the FCDO names no advisory against travel to Uganda. *https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda — page updated 2026-07-27.*","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Will this clear - should I wait for Kibale?","a":"Possibly - this is a health-driven, dynamic advisory (an outbreak, not conflict), so it can be lifted when the outbreak is contained. We re-verify Uganda''s status every publish cycle and will flip Kibale to bookable the moment it drops below Level 4. For a firm 2026 chimp trek, book Nyungwe now.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What would Kibale offer when it reopens?","a":"The primate capital of the world - up to 1,500 chimps and 13 primate species, the $250 chimp trek (and the full-day ~$300 Habituation Experience), plus the Bigodi wetland birding walk. All held until the advisory lifts.","source":"gorillatrackers.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"Is Kibale a safari (big-game) destination?","a":"No - it is a rainforest of primates, not a savanna, so big-game safari is a documented miss; the draw is the chimp and primate trek (a Global Adventures product), exactly like Rwanda''s Nyungwe. For Big game, we route to Kenya, Tanzania or Akagera.","source":"gorillatrackers.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"What are the non-Ebola health requirements for Uganda?","a":"Yellow fever is mandatory for entry (all travelers >=1 yr, checked at Entebbe, vaccinate >=10 days before); malaria prophylaxis is essential (all regions); carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance. All moot while the L4 hold stands.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Kibale Forest, Uganda: Chimpanzee Trekking in the Primate Capital - On Hold (Level 4 / Ebola)","meta_description":"Kibale Forest National Park - the ''primate capital of the world,'' up to 1,500 chimpanzees and 13 primate species, the $250 chimp trek and the full-day Habituation Experience - is currently a US Level 4 ''Do Not Travel'' zone (Ebola outbreak). What it is, why it''s held, and where to trek chimps instead (Rwanda''s Nyungwe Forest).","slug":"kibale-forest-uganda","primary_keyword":"Kibale Forest chimpanzee trekking","long_tail":["Kibale chimpanzee permit cost 2026","chimpanzee habituation experience Uganda","Kibale primate capital","Bigodi wetland walk","is Uganda safe Ebola","Kibale vs Nyungwe"],"search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Kibale","chimpanzee","Bigodi","Magombe","Kanyanchu","red colobus"],"hreflang":["en"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-01"},"booking":{"bin":"booking_hold","level":"L4","codes":["do-not-travel","ebola-sudan-virus-pheic","health-outbreak"],"book_suppressed":true,"waiver":false,"dynamic":true,"note":"Uganda US L4 Do Not Travel driven by an Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. CONTENT-ONLY, Book button suppressed, no waiver. DYNAMIC health advisory - re-verify EVERY publish cycle; flip to live the moment it drops below L4. Redirect live chimp-trek demand to nyungwe-forest-rwanda (Rwanda, bookable, US L3 - the direct live twin)."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":6,"misses":16,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; EVERY hit is HELD behind the L4 booking hold - no SI is servable while Level 4 stands; per the safari-build rule the chimp trek is globaladv (PRIMARY here) - safari (big game) is a documented MISS on a rainforest; birding/13-primates = deepdive; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"held","note":"chimp trek + full-day Habituation Experience (PRIMARY)"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"held","note":"13 primate species / birding"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"held"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"held","note":"Bigodi wetland community walk"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Kyaninga Lodge / Ndali Lodge (HELD)","why_ultra":"the area''s apex stays - hand-built log-and-crater-lake lodges above the forest; documented for the day the hold lifts, sold by no one today","earning":"none while held","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"n/a (L4 booking hold)","tier":"ultra","status":"HELD"},{"name":"A private double-chimp + Habituation + Bigodi week (HELD)","why_ultra":"the standard trek + the full-day habituation + the 13 primates + the Bigodi wetland, privately guided - latent","earning":"none while held","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"n/a (L4 booking hold)","tier":"ultra","status":"HELD"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Kibale Forest National Park, Uganda"},"geo":{"lat":0.49,"lng":30.39}}'::jsonb, 6),
  ('laikipia-kenya', '05A', 'Laikipia Plateau', 'Kenya', 'Kenya''s conservancy country', 'live', 'verified', 'lion', 'Kenya — Laikipia Plateau', '{"safari","ultra","adventure","romance","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Kenya''s private-conservancy heartland (Ol Pejeta, Lewa, Borana, Loisaba, Solio) - low-density, exclusive; the LAST TWO northern white rhinos on Earth (Najin + Fatu, Ol Pejeta, on-site IVF programme)","Ol Pejeta (90,000 acres) = largest black-rhino population in East Africa + Sweetwaters Chimpanzee Sanctuary (only chimps in Kenya); Lewa (UNESCO 2013) = ~12% of Kenya''s black rhino + largest Grevy''s zebra population","Do-more safari on private land: horseback safaris, walking safaris (armed guide), night drives, lion tracking, mountain biking, camel treks, star beds - all banned in the national parks","US L2 Exercise Increased Caution (elevated risk Nairobi/urban, not the conservancies); best Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar but rewarding year-round - the anchor when migration parks peak-price","Sold via Kenya safari DMCs at a FAVOURABLE 15-22% - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; conservancy/conservation fees non-commissionable pass-through","KES (~129/USD) + M-Pesa but safari quoted USD; eTA required; malaria lower at ~1,800m but present (prophylaxis advised); YF only if arriving from a risk country; AMREF for the on-foot/horse activities"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 / 112 (limited in remote areas); Kenya Red Cross ambulance 1199; AMREF Flying Doctors for bush evac","hospital":"Remote plateau - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d, air evac) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Nanyuki/Nairobi","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"lower at ~1,800m but present - prophylaxis advised (chloroquine-resistant); DEET at dusk","yellow_fever":"compulsory only if arriving from a risk country; CDC recommends for most","activity_note":"L2 disclose (elevated risk is Nairobi/urban, not the conservancies). Signature on-foot/on-horse/night safaris among dangerous game - armed conservancy guides only, higher-risk than a vehicle, follow instruction. Remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to: Mandera County Tarbaj and Wajir East constituencies in Wajir County, except for Wajir Town areas of Wajir County within 60km of Kenya’s border with Somalia Garissa County - except for Garissa Town, the constituency of Lagdera and the areas of Balambala constituency which lie north and west of the main road which runs from Saka on the Tana River up to the intersection with the C81 Road Lamu County, except for Lamu Island and Manda Island FCDO advises against all but essential travel to: Garissa Town Tana River County north of the Tana River as far as the town of Saka within 15km of the east coast between the Tana River and the Galana (Athi-Galana-Sabaki) River Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to: Mandera County Tarbaj and Wajir East constituencies in Wajir County, except for Wajir Town areas of Wajir County within 60km of Kenya’s border with Somalia Garissa County - except for Garissa Town, the constituency of Lagdera and the areas of Balambala constituency which lie north and west of the main road which runs from Saka on the Tana River up to the intersection with the C81 Road Lamu County, except for Lamu Island and Manda Island FCDO advises against all but essential travel to: Garissa Town Tana River County north of the Tana River as far as the town of Saka within 15km of the east coast between the Tana River and the Galana (Athi-Galana-Sabaki) River There have been frequent attacks in the north-eastern border regions, most of which were attributed to Al Shabaab."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to: Garissa Town Tana River County north of the Tana River as far as the town of Saka within 15km of the east coast between the Tana River and the Galana (Athi-Galana-Sabaki) River Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to: Garissa Town Tana River County north of the Tana River as far as the town of Saka within 15km of the east coast between the Tana River and the Galana (Athi-Galana-Sabaki) River There have been frequent attacks in the north-eastern border regions, most of which were attributed to Al Shabaab."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-06-24T12:48:44+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar (dry) - best game + activities; conservancy camps busiest but low-density caps keep it quiet","shoulder":"Jun + Nov (good, softer rates)","green":"Apr-May (long rains - lush, quiet, cheapest; plateau still delivers)","booking_lead":"conservancy lodges 4-9 mo (Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar; camps small + capped); shoulder 2-4 mo; green 1-2 mo","off_season_specials":"Apr-May green-season value; the year-round anchor when migration parks peak-price; combine Samburu (Special Five) or the Mara","event_peaks":"Jul-Oct + Christmas/NY + Easter; Lewa Safari Marathon (~Jun, verify) spikes Lewa","campaign_start":"conservancy weeks 6-9 mo out; market year-round + green value vs the migration-park price crush; bundle Laikipia (rhino) + Amboseli/Mara to complete the Big Five"},"jewels":[{"name":"The last two northern white rhinos (Ol Pejeta)","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$600-2,000/pp/day","timing":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"stand beside Najin and Fatu — the last two northern white rhinos on Earth","si":"safari","blurb":"stand beside Najin and Fatu — the last two northern white rhinos on Earth","when":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar","commission":"conservancy DMC 15-22%"},{"name":"A low-density Big-Five conservancy safari","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$600-2,500/pp/day","timing":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Big Five with a fraction of the vehicles across Ol Pejeta/Lewa/Borana/Loisaba — plus Lewa''s endangered Grevy''s zebra — the exclusive, quiet Kenya","si":"safari","blurb":"Big Five with a fraction of the vehicles across Ol Pejeta/Lewa/Borana/Loisaba — plus Lewa''s endangered Grevy''s zebra — the exclusive, quiet Kenya","when":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar","commission":"conservancy DMC 15-22%"},{"name":"Horseback + walking + night safari","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$50-300/pp","timing":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"track lion on foot, ride among the zebra, and drive after dark for leopard","si":"adventure","blurb":"track lion on foot, ride among the zebra, and drive after dark for leopard","when":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar","commission":"conservancy DMC"},{"name":"Rhino conservation + Sweetwaters chimps","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$40-200/pp","timing":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"behind-the-scenes conservation tours, the northern-white-rhino IVF story, and Kenya''s only chimpanzees at Sweetwaters — a genuine conservation deep-dive","si":"deepdive","blurb":"behind-the-scenes conservation tours, the northern-white-rhino IVF story, and Kenya''s only chimpanzees at Sweetwaters — a genuine conservation deep-dive","when":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar","commission":"conservancy/DMC"},{"name":"A conservancy luxury honeymoon (Loisaba / Segera / Borana)","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$800-3,000+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 4-9 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Laikipia''s apex camps — Loisaba''s star beds, Segera''s art-filled sanctuary, Borana''s Big-Five ridge — private, exclusive and activity-rich; honeymoon-grade","si":"ultra","blurb":"Laikipia''s apex camps — Loisaba''s star beds, Segera''s art-filled sanctuary, Borana''s Big-Five ridge — private, exclusive and activity-rich; honeymoon-grade","when":"standing; peak 4-9 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC"},{"name":"A Laikipia conservancy honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jul-Oct + Dec-Mar","commission":"consortia/host"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Laikipia?","a":"The on-foot and on-horse activities, and remoteness. Laikipia''s draw is walking, horseback and night safaris among dangerous game - inherently higher-risk than a vehicle; go only with the armed conservancy guides and follow instruction. The plateau is remote, so carry AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30 days) + travel-medical insurance.","source":"africanmeccasafaris.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Where do I see rhino - and the last two northern whites?","a":"At Ol Pejeta (the last two northern white rhinos, Najin and Fatu, in a guarded 700-acre enclosure, plus East Africa''s largest black-rhino population) and Lewa (~12% of Kenya''s black rhino, plus Grevy''s zebra) - the best rhino viewing in Kenya, and a genuine conservation story.","source":"expertafrica.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Laikipia?","a":"Jun/Jul-Oct and Dec-Mar (dry) are best, but the high plateau delivers year-round - a strong choice when the migration parks are at their peak-price crush. The green season is lush, quiet and better value.","source":"safaribookings.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"What can I do in Laikipia that I can''t in the national parks?","a":"Because it''s private conservancy land: horseback safaris, walking safaris, night drives, lion tracking, mountain biking, camel treks and star beds - the active, immersive safari the parks don''t allow, with a fraction of the vehicles.","source":"asiliaafrica.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Kenya?","a":"An eTA (Kenya replaced visas with the eTA in 2024 - apply at least 2 weeks ahead). Yellow fever is compulsory only if you arrive from a YF-risk country; CDC recommends the vaccine for most.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safari"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Laikipia Safari Guide: Ol Pejeta, the Last Northern White Rhinos, Conservancies & Best Time","meta_description":"Plan a Laikipia safari - Kenya''s private-conservancy heartland: the last two northern white rhinos at Ol Pejeta, East Africa''s biggest black-rhino sanctuary, Lewa''s Grevy''s zebra, Kenya''s only chimps, and low-density safari you can do on foot, horseback or after dark - with real safety, timing and cost.","slug":"laikipia-kenya","primary_keyword":"Laikipia safari","long_tail":["Ol Pejeta northern white rhino","Laikipia conservancies","Lewa Wildlife Conservancy","Sweetwaters chimpanzee sanctuary","horseback safari Kenya","best time Laikipia","is Laikipia safe"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Laikipia","Ol Pejeta","faru weupe","Lewa","Sweetwaters","safari ya farasi","punda milia wa Grevy"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-31"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":["exercise-increased-caution","crime","urban-unrest"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Kenya US L2 Exercise Increased Caution - elevated risk in Nairobi/urban areas, not the Laikipia conservancies (low-density, strong security); safe licensed-operator safari. Disclose L2. Re-verify each cycle."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; SAFARI is the launch/demo SI - primary safari not globaladv; horseback + walking + night drives + biking + camel = globaladv (standing horseback/adventure rule); rhino-conservation/chimp story = deepdive; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"Big Five, rhino sanctuaries, Grevy''s"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"conservancy luxury lodges"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"horseback, walking, night drives, lion tracking, biking, camel"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"rhino conservation / Sweetwaters chimps"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Segera Retreat / Loisaba - the plateau''s apex stays","why_ultra":"art-filled sanctuary suites + famous star beds, private guiding, horseback + walking across a vast private wilderness","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,500-3,000+/night"},{"name":"A private conservancy do-more week (ride, walk, track, sleep out)","why_ultra":"exclusive-use camp with private guiding, horseback + walking safaris, night drives + a star-bed night","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"A Big-Five-completing week (Laikipia rhino + Amboseli + Mara)","why_ultra":"rhino in Laikipia + elephants-and-Kili in Amboseli + the migration in the Mara, private-guided fly-in throughout","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-31","hero":{"query":"Laikipia Plateau, Kenya"},"geo":{"lat":0.2,"lng":36.9}}'::jsonb, 7)
insert into public.destinations (id, region_code, name, country, line, status, depth, img, sub_region, si, feel, tier_range, price_band, draw_rank, data, position) values
  ('lake-manyara-tanzania', '05A', 'Lake Manyara National Park', 'Tanzania', 'Lions in the acacias, a lake pink with a', 'live', 'verified', 'lion', 'Tanzania — Northern Safari Circuit', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","romance","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["The only park in Tanzania where lions habitually climb trees (tree-climbing lions) - the signature sight - beneath the Great Rift Valley escarpment","A flamingo lake: the alkaline soda lake is two-thirds of the ~330 km2 park and draws up to ~1.9 million flamingos feeding on its algae, plus 370+ bird species","A compact habitat mosaic (groundwater forest, acacia woodland, grassland, lake) with 60+ mammals - big elephant/buffalo herds, huge baboon troops, hippos, giraffe; four of the Big Five (no rhino)","US L3 Reconsider Travel - terrorism concern is the Mtwara Region (far southern coast, far from the northern circuit); bookable with L3 disclosure + consent; disclose LGBTQ+ targeting; travel with a licensed operator","The gateway to Ngorongoro - the classic first-morning/half-day stop; best Jun-Oct for game/tree-climbing lions, Nov-Jun for the biggest flamingo flocks; permits a treetop canopy walk + night drive + cycling + kayak","Sold via Tanzanian safari DMCs + camp consortia 10-20%+ - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; TANAPA park fees + activity fees pass-through; TZS (~2,633/USD, USD is the safari currency); eVisa; AMREF for evac"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 999","hospital":"Remote/bush - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Arusha","advisory_level":"L3","malaria":"present (lower on the northern circuit but real at the lake''s lower elevation) - prophylaxis + DEET advised","yellow_fever":"not required direct from US/Europe; mandatory if transiting >12h through a risk country (e.g. Kenya)","activity_note":"L3 DISCLOSE + CONSENT (terrorism concern is the far-southern Mtwara Region, far away; disclose LGBTQ+ targeting - same-sex relations criminalized; travel with a licensed operator). On safari: keep clear of the large bold baboon troops (don''t feed, secure food), stay in-vehicle near lions/elephants, canopy walkway railed/guided, night drive to vehicle rules. Remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to parts of Tanzania Tanzania FCDO advises against all but essential travel to any area within 20km of the Tanzanian border with the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, due to attacks by groups linked with Islamic extremism."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to any area within 20km of the Tanzanian border with the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, due to attacks by groups linked with Islamic extremism."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Oct (dry) - best game + tree-climbing lions; rides the northern-circuit high season; book 3-6 mo ahead","shoulder":"Nov + Feb-Mar (good rates, flamingo flocks building, fewer vehicles)","green":"Apr-May (long rains - lush, birdy, cheapest; forest greenest)","booking_lead":"camps 3-6 mo for Jun-Oct; green 1-2 mo","off_season_specials":"wet-season flamingo + birding spectacle (Nov-Jun, biggest flocks); the canopy walk as a green-season family draw","event_peaks":"Jul-Sep + Christmas/NY; the flamingo season","campaign_start":"Jun-Oct 4-6 mo out as the northern-circuit gateway stop; flamingo/birding value Nov-Jun; position as the compact scene-stealer on the road to the Crater"},"jewels":[{"name":"The tree-climbing lions","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"camp + park fees","timing":"Jun-Oct best","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Lake Manyara is the only place in Tanzania where lions habitually lounge in trees — draped along acacia branches above the plains","si":"safari","blurb":"Lake Manyara is the only place in Tanzania where lions habitually lounge in trees — draped along acacia branches above the plains","when":"Jun-Oct best","commission":"DMC/camp"},{"name":"Forest elephants + the Rift-wall scene","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"camp + park fees","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"elephants moving through cool groundwater forest beneath a thousand-foot escarpment, hippo pools and giraffe on the flats","si":"safari","blurb":"elephants moving through cool groundwater forest beneath a thousand-foot escarpment, hippo pools and giraffe on the flats","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC/camp"},{"name":"Treetop canopy walk + night drive + kayak","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$25-200/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a railed canopy walkway through the forest, spotlit night drives for nocturnal cats, cycling the escarpment and kayaking among the flamingos","si":"adventure","blurb":"a railed canopy walkway through the forest, spotlit night drives for nocturnal cats, cycling the escarpment and kayaking among the flamingos","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC"},{"name":"The flamingo lake + a 370-bird list","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Nov-Jun best for flamingos","draw_rank":1,"hook":"up to 1.9 million flamingos on an algae-rich soda lake, plus 370 bird species across four habitats","si":"deepdive","blurb":"up to 1.9 million flamingos on an algae-rich soda lake, plus 370 bird species across four habitats","when":"Nov-Jun best for flamingos","commission":"DMC/specialist"},{"name":"A Lake Manyara Tree Lodge honeymoon","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$1,000-2,200+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 3-6 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"&Beyond''s stilted treehouse suites in the mahogany forest — the only luxury lodge inside the park","si":"ultra","blurb":"&Beyond''s stilted treehouse suites in the mahogany forest — the only luxury lodge inside the park","when":"standing; peak 3-6 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC"},{"name":"A Lake Manyara honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"&Beyond''s stilted treehouse suites in the mahogany forest — the only luxury lodge inside the park","si":"romance","blurb":"&Beyond''s stilted treehouse suites in the mahogany forest — the only luxury lodge inside the park","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"consortia/host"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Lake Manyara?","a":"Not the parks - the advisory''s concerns are the far-southern Mtwara Region (terrorism, far away) and city petty crime, plus a flagged LGBTQ+ targeting concern travelers should weigh (Tanzanian law criminalizes same-sex relations). In Manyara itself the risks are ordinary safari ones: stay in-vehicle near game, keep clear of the large baboon troops, malaria prophylaxis.","source":"newsweek.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the tree-climbing lions guaranteed?","a":"No sighting is ever guaranteed - the tree-climbing behaviour is famous but sporadic - yet Manyara is the one park in Tanzania where it happens regularly, and even without it the park''s flamingos, forest, elephants and Rift-wall scenery justify the stop.","source":"africanscenicsafaris.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Lake Manyara?","a":"For game and the tree-climbing lions, the dry season Jun-Oct; for the flamingo spectacle and birding, the wetter Nov-Jun when the lake fills and the algae blooms draw the biggest flocks. It''s a rewarding stop year-round.","source":"africanscenicsafaris.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Is Manyara worth more than a half-day?","a":"For most itineraries it''s a half-day or overnight gateway stop en route to Ngorongoro - that''s the right dose for a compact park - but birders and photographers happily give it a full day for the forest, the lake hide and the escarpment light.","source":"africageographic.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Tanzania?","a":"eVisa required - apply on the official portal before departure. Yellow fever is not required direct from the US/Europe, but is mandatory if you transit >12 h through a risk country like Kenya.","source":"tanzania-specialist.com","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Lake Manyara National Park Guide: Tree-Climbing Lions, Flamingos & Best Time","meta_description":"Plan a Lake Manyara safari - the northern circuit''s compact scene-stealer: Tanzania''s only tree-climbing lions, up to 1.9 million flamingos, a groundwater forest and canopy walkway beneath the Rift escarpment - with the US Level-3 advisory, best time, activities and where to stay en route to Ngorongoro.","slug":"lake-manyara-tanzania","primary_keyword":"Lake Manyara tree-climbing lions","long_tail":["Lake Manyara flamingos","Lake Manyara canopy walkway","Lake Manyara best time to visit","Lake Manyara vs Ngorongoro","is Tanzania safe safari","Lake Manyara birding"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Manyara","simba","flamingo","msitu","nyani"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-01"},"booking":{"bin":"book_with_disclosure","level":"L3","codes":["reconsider-travel","mtwara-terrorism-carveout-far","lgbtq-targeting"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Tanzania US L3 Reconsider Travel - the terrorism concern is the Mtwara Region (far southern coast), far from the northern circuit. Bookable with L3 disclosure + consent; also disclose the LGBTQ+ targeting consideration (same-sex relations criminalized). Travel with a licensed operator. Re-verify each cycle."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":6,"misses":16,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; per the safari-build rule big game (tree-climbing lions) is safari (PRIMARY here), NOT globaladv; canopy walk + night drive + cycling + kayak = globaladv; flamingos/370 birds = deepdive; no rhino (four of Big Five); sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"big-game - Tanzania''s only reliable tree-climbing lions (PRIMARY)"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"treetop canopy walk + night drive + cycling + kayak"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"&Beyond Lake Manyara Tree Lodge"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"flamingos / 370 birds"}],"ultra":[{"name":"&Beyond Lake Manyara Tree Lodge - the in-park apex","why_ultra":"stilted treehouse suites in an ancient mahogany forest, the only luxury lodge inside the park, with private guiding","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,000-2,200+/night"},{"name":"A private Manyara forest-and-flamingo day","why_ultra":"an exclusive-guide loop: the tree-climbing lions + the canopy walk + the lake hide + a kayak among the flamingos, from an ultra lodge","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"The Manyara gateway leg of a private northern-circuit safari","why_ultra":"Manyara + Tarangire + Ngorongoro + Serengeti, privately guided and flown","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Lake Manyara National Park, Tanzania"},"geo":{"lat":-3.5833,"lng":35.8333}}'::jsonb, 8),
  ('lalibela-ethiopia', '05A', 'Lalibela', 'Ethiopia', 'Eleven churches carved from living rock', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Horn & Highlands', '{"culture","deepdive","pilgrimage"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"posture":"no-booking","zone":"The Amhara Region","booking_hold":true,"notes":"FCDO advises against all travel to parts of Ethiopia, including the Amhara region, in which Lalibela sits. We do not book this destination. SINGLE SOURCE: travel.state.gov returned HTTP 403 on a fourth attempt (2026-08-16), so no US level was obtained.","source":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office — Ethiopia travel advice","verified":"2026-05-29","emergency":"991 police · 907 ambulance (Red Cross) · 911 general","malaria":"Active outbreak across all 14 regions; transmission below ~2,500 m. Lalibela sits at ~2,500 m; lowland transit legs carry risk and chemoprophylaxis is advised.","yellow_fever":"Proof required if arriving from or transiting more than 12 hours in a yellow-fever risk country; not required direct from the US. CDC recommends the vaccine for travellers 9 months and over.","activity_note":"Steep church steps, dark interconnecting tunnels and uneven rock. Mild altitude at ~2,500 m; the Asheton Maryam monastery hike rises above 3,000 m."},"timing":null,"jewels":[{"name":"Bete Giyorgis, the Church of St George","tier":"essential","si":"culture","blurb":"A perfectly symmetrical Greek-cross monolith hewn about 12 m down into the rock, the best-preserved of the eleven.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_of_Saint_George,_Lalibela"},{"name":"The two interconnected church clusters","tier":"essential","si":"culture","blurb":"Eleven medieval monolithic churches carved from solid rock in the late 12th to early 13th century, UNESCO-listed in 1978.","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/18/"},{"name":"Genna at Lalibela","tier":"essential","si":"pilgrimage","blurb":"Ethiopian Christmas on 7 January, when the rock-hewn churches fill with the chant of a living faith.","source":"https://www.brilliant-ethiopia.com/christmas-in-lalibela"},{"name":"The Asheton Maryam monastery hike","tier":"comfort","si":"deepdive","blurb":"A climb above 3,000 m to a monastery in the cliffs over the town.","source":"https://www.brilliant-ethiopia.com/asheton-maryam-monastery-lalibela"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can I book a trip to Lalibela through TravelWell?","a":"No. FCDO advises against all travel to parts of Ethiopia, including the Amhara region, in which Lalibela sits. We do not book this destination. SINGLE SOURCE: travel.state.gov returned HTTP 403 on a fourth attempt (2026-08-16), so no US level was obtained. The page stays open because the place is worth knowing about; the booking path does not.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ethiopia"},{"q":"What is Lalibela?","a":"Eleven medieval monolithic churches carved straight down into solid volcanic rock in the late 12th to early 13th century, UNESCO-listed in 1978 and still a living Orthodox worship site. It was conceived as a New Jerusalem so Ethiopian Christians could make pilgrimage at home after Muslim conquests cut off the Holy Land.","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/18/"},{"q":"When do the churches fill with pilgrims?","a":"At Genna, Ethiopian Christmas, on 7 January. The dry season runs October to March at roughly 15 to 25C.","source":"https://www.brilliant-ethiopia.com/christmas-in-lalibela"},{"q":"What are the emergency numbers in Ethiopia?","a":"991 for police, 907 for the Red Cross ambulance, 911 general. An older note circulating as 939 is the fire service, not an ambulance.","source":"https://addisababa.embassy.qa/en/ethiopia/important-numbers"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Lalibela, Ethiopia — the rock-hewn churches | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Eleven medieval monolithic churches carved from living rock, UNESCO-listed in 1978, still a living Orthodox pilgrimage site. Why we do not currently book Ethiopia''s Amhara region.","slug":"lalibela-ethiopia","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"TravelWell.World research","content_freshness":"2026-08-16","primary_keyword":"Lalibela rock-hewn churches"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["culture","deepdive","pilgrimage"],"ultra":null,"source_verified":"2026-08-16","hero":{"query":"Lalibela, Ethiopia"},"geo":{"lat":12.0361,"lng":39.0457},"geo_source":"https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?q=Lalibela,+Ethiopia — OpenStreetMap Nominatim, place/town, North Wollo, Amhara, 2026","geo_accessed":"2026-08-18"}'::jsonb, 9),
  ('murchison-falls-uganda', '05A', 'Murchison Falls National Park', 'Uganda', 'The world''s most powerful waterfall, four of the Big', 'future', 'verified', 'safariJeep', 'Uganda — Murchison Falls / Nile', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["BOOKING HOLD: Uganda US L4 Do Not Travel driven by an Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. CONTENT-ONLY, no Book path, no waiver. DYNAMIC - re-verify each cycle, flip to live when it clears. Redirect safari demand to Kenya/Tanzania/Akagera","Uganda''s largest park (~3,840 km2), bisected by the Victoria Nile which funnels through a 7-m gorge and plunges 43 m - often called the world''s most powerful waterfall","The Big Four (lion, elephant, buffalo, leopard - NO rhino in-park; rhino at the separate Ziwa Rhino Sanctuary en route) + endangered Nubian giraffe, across 76+ mammals; 450+ birds incl. the shoebill","The Nile boat safari to the base of the falls ($30) - hippos, giant crocs, elephants, buffalo; delta shoebill cruise; the top-of-falls hike","Park fee $40 (24h); yellow fever MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe); eVisa (no visa-on-arrival); ~300 km / 4h NW of Kampala; malaria in all regions (prophylaxis)","Live twins = Kenya (Maasai Mara/Amboseli L2), Tanzania (Serengeti L3), akagera-np-rwanda (Rwanda Big Five L3). Anchors the Uganda cluster with bwindi/queen-elizabeth/kibale"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 / 112","hospital":"Remote - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Masindi/Gulu/Kampala","malaria":"present in all regions - prophylaxis","yellow_fever":"MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe, >=10 days before)","ebola":"Sudan virus outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. Health information, not an advisory against travel - the FCDO restricts nothing in Uganda; re-verify current outbreak status before travel","activity_note":"Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak is standing health information to re-verify each cycle - not a booking hold (health-based holds released, David 2026-08-29). Top-of-falls behind railings/guides, keep back from hippos/crocs on the Nile boat, standard game-drive rules","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the DRC provinces that border Uganda."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to these DRC provinces."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the provinces of DRC that border Uganda, including Virunga National Park."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to South Sudan."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-27T15:00:28+01:00"}},"timing":{"booking_status":"HELD - no live demand capture while Level 4 stands (no campaigns/fire-dates)","latent_peak":"Dec-Feb + Jun-Sep (drier - game near the Nile, firmer tracks) - IF cleared","latent_green":"Mar-May + Oct-Nov (rains, lush/birdy, softer rates; falls fullest after rain)","latent_booking_lead":"lodges 2-4 mo peak - NOT applicable while held","reverify_trigger":"check Uganda''s advisory EVERY publish cycle - DYNAMIC health advisory; flip to live the moment it drops below L4","redirect":"live safari demand -> Kenya (Maasai Mara/Amboseli L2) / Tanzania (Serengeti L3) / akagera-np-rwanda (Rwanda Big Five L3)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Big-Four game on the Nile plains","si_tag":"safari","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD; latent Dec-Feb + Jun-Sep","draw_rank":null,"hook":"four of the Big Five — lion, elephant, buffalo, leopard — plus herds of the endangered Nubian giraffe across Uganda''s largest park","si":"safari","blurb":"four of the Big Five — lion, elephant, buffalo, leopard — plus herds of the endangered Nubian giraffe across Uganda''s largest park","when":"HELD; latent Dec-Feb + Jun-Sep","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"The Nile boat safari to the base of the falls","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"held","tier":"essential","price_band":"HELD (Nile boat $30 latent)","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"a boat cruise up the Victoria Nile to the foot of the thundering falls","si":"adventure","blurb":"a boat cruise up the Victoria Nile to the foot of the thundering falls","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"The top-of-the-falls hike","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"held","tier":"essential","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"a short, steep walk to the lip where the entire Nile is squeezed through a 7-m slot and hurled 43 m","si":"adventure","blurb":"a short, steep walk to the lip where the entire Nile is squeezed through a 7-m slot and hurled 43 m","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"A shoebill + 450-bird delta","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"the Nile delta is one of the best places on Earth to see the prehistoric, statue-still shoebill","si":"deepdive","blurb":"the Nile delta is one of the best places on Earth to see the prehistoric, statue-still shoebill","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"A Nile safari-lodge honeymoon (held)","si_tag":"ultra","status":"held","tier":"comfort","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"Nile Safari Lodge and Baker''s Lodge on the river''s edge, Paraa and Chobe overlooking the water","si":"ultra","blurb":"Nile Safari Lodge and Baker''s Lodge on the river''s edge, Paraa and Chobe overlooking the water","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Where can I go on safari instead, right now?","a":"Kenya (Maasai Mara / Amboseli, US L2, bookable) or Tanzania (Serengeti / Ngorongoro, US L3, bookable) for the classic Big-game plains - or Akagera, Rwanda (US L3, a Big-Five comeback ~2h from Kigali) for the nearest live savanna. We route all Uganda safari demand there.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Will this clear - should I wait for Murchison?","a":"Possibly - this is a health-driven, dynamic advisory (an outbreak, not conflict), so it can be lifted when the outbreak is contained. We re-verify Uganda''s status every publish cycle and will flip the park to bookable the moment it drops below Level 4. For a firm 2026 safari, book Kenya, Tanzania or Akagera now.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What would Murchison offer when it reopens?","a":"Uganda''s largest park - the world''s most powerful waterfall (the Nile through a 7-m gorge), four of the Big Five plus Nubian giraffe, the Nile boat safari to the falls'' base, delta shoebill cruises and a top-of-falls hike. All held until the advisory lifts.","source":"mustseespots.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Is there rhino - is it a Big Five park?","a":"Four of the five: lion, elephant, buffalo and leopard live in the park - no rhino in Murchison itself. Rhino are seen at the separate Ziwa Rhino Sanctuary on the drive up from Kampala (also held while Uganda is L4).","source":"worldblossomsafari.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"What are the non-Ebola health requirements for Uganda?","a":"Yellow fever is mandatory for entry (all travelers >=1 yr, checked at Entebbe, vaccinate >=10 days before); malaria prophylaxis is essential (all regions); carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance. All moot while the L4 hold stands.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Murchison Falls NP, Uganda: The World''s Most Powerful Waterfall & Nile Safari - On Hold (Level 4 / Ebola)","meta_description":"Murchison Falls National Park - Uganda''s largest park: the world''s most powerful waterfall (the Nile through a 7-m gorge), four of the Big Five, the Nile boat safari and shoebill delta - is currently a US Level 4 ''Do Not Travel'' zone (Ebola outbreak). What it is, why it''s held, and where to safari instead (Kenya, Tanzania, Rwanda''s Akagera).","slug":"murchison-falls-uganda","primary_keyword":"Murchison Falls National Park safari","long_tail":["Murchison Falls Nile boat cruise","world''s most powerful waterfall","Murchison Big Four","shoebill Murchison delta","is Uganda safe Ebola","Murchison vs Serengeti"],"search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Murchison","Kabalega Falls","Victoria Nile","Paraa","shoebill","Nubian giraffe"],"hreflang":["en"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-01"},"booking":{"bin":"booking_hold","level":"L4","codes":["do-not-travel","ebola-sudan-virus-pheic","health-outbreak"],"book_suppressed":true,"waiver":false,"dynamic":true,"note":"Uganda US L4 Do Not Travel driven by an Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. CONTENT-ONLY, Book button suppressed, no waiver. DYNAMIC health advisory - re-verify EVERY publish cycle; flip to live the moment it drops below L4. Redirect live safari demand to Kenya (Maasai Mara/Amboseli L2), Tanzania (Serengeti L3), akagera-np-rwanda (Rwanda Big Five L3)."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":6,"misses":16,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; EVERY hit is HELD behind the L4 booking hold - no SI is servable while Level 4 stands; safari = Big-Four game (primary when live), globaladv = Nile boat safari + top-of-falls hike; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"held","note":"Big-Four game (lion/elephant/buffalo/leopard) + Nubian giraffe"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"held","note":"Nile boat safari to the base of the falls + top-of-falls hike"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"held"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"held","note":"shoebill / 450+ birds"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Nile Safari Lodge / Baker''s Lodge (HELD)","why_ultra":"the park''s apex stays - barefoot-luxury bandas on the Nile''s edge; documented for the day the hold lifts, sold by no one today","earning":"none while held","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"n/a (L4 booking hold)","tier":"ultra","status":"HELD"},{"name":"A private falls + Nile + delta + Ziwa-rhino week (HELD)","why_ultra":"the top-of-falls hike + the boat to the base + the shoebill delta + a Ziwa rhino add-on en route, privately guided - latent","earning":"none while held","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"n/a (L4 booking hold)","tier":"ultra","status":"HELD"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Murchison Falls National Park, Uganda"},"geo":{"lat":2.2,"lng":31.8}}'::jsonb, 10),
  ('ngorongoro-crater-tanzania', '05A', 'Ngorongoro Crater', 'Tanzania', 'The world''s largest caldera', 'live', 'verified', 'safariJeep', 'Tanzania — Northern Safari Circuit / Ngorongoro', '{"safari","ultra","romance","deepdive","culture","adventure"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["World''s largest intact volcanic caldera (UNESCO 1979) - 600-m walls, 2-3 M years old; ~25,000 large mammals at Africa''s highest predator density","The best Big-Five-in-one-day in Africa (lion, elephant, buffalo, leopard, resident black rhino <30); ideal first safari","Olduvai Gorge (cradle of mankind - Homo habilis, ~3.6 M-year fossils) within the Conservation Area; Maasai coexist and graze the highlands","Game dense YEAR-ROUND (animals stay in the crater); dry Jun-Oct clearest, Jan-Feb greener/quieter, Apr-May cheapest; usually 1 crater day in a Northern-Circuit loop","US L3 Reconsider Travel (terrorism = Mtwara far south, NOT the circuit; LGBTQ+ flagged); NCAA fees pass-through ($70.80/adult + $295/vehicle descent + VAT); sold via safari DMCs IATAN-not-CLIA","TZS but USD is the safari currency; eVisa; malaria prophylaxis advised (lower at rim); Seneto descent ~600m steep; AMREF Flying Doctors for evac"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 999 (unreliable outside cities; no reliable govt ambulance - rely on camp/operator radio + AMREF Flying Doctors)","hospital":"Remote - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Arusha","advisory_level":"L3","malaria":"prophylaxis advised - lower at the 2,200-2,300m rim but the floor/surrounds are malarial; DEET at dusk","yellow_fever":"not required from a non-risk country; mandatory if transiting >12h a risk country (e.g. Kenya)","activity_note":"L3 DISCLOSE + CONSENT (terrorism = Mtwara far south, NOT the circuit; LGBTQ+ targeting flagged). Dangerous game at close range on the floor - stay in the vehicle, follow the guide. Seneto descent ~600m steep/narrow (dry conditions, 4x4). Rim altitude ~2,200-2,300m mild effects. Remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to parts of Tanzania Tanzania FCDO advises against all but essential travel to any area within 20km of the Tanzanian border with the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, due to attacks by groups linked with Islamic extremism."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to any area within 20km of the Tanzanian border with the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, due to attacks by groups linked with Islamic extremism."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Oct (dry, clearest viewing) + Dec-Feb (holiday + Serengeti-calving combo)","shoulder":"Nov + Mar (quieter, softer rates, good game)","green":"Apr-May (long rains - green, quietest, cheapest)","booking_lead":"rim lodges + Northern-Circuit 6-12 mo for Jun-Oct + Dec-Feb (crater-rim luxury sells out); shoulder 3-6 mo; green 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"Apr-May green-season value; combine Serengeti calving (Jan-Feb) or Tarangire/Manyara","event_peaks":"Jun-Oct high season + Christmas/NY + Easter; daily-vehicle-cap makes peak floor access tight","campaign_start":"Jun-Oct loops 9-12 mo out; Jan-Feb calving+crater combos by prior Apr-Jun; green-season value by prior Nov-Dec"},"jewels":[{"name":"The Big-Five crater-floor game drive","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~$700-2,000/pp/day","timing":"year-round; dry Jun-Oct clearest","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the most reliable Big-Five day in Africa — lion, elephant, buffalo, leopard and rhino on one grassy floor at the continent''s highest predator density","si":"safari","blurb":"the most reliable Big-Five day in Africa — lion, elephant, buffalo, leopard and rhino on one grassy floor at the continent''s highest predator density","when":"year-round; dry Jun-Oct clearest","commission":"safari DMC 10-15%"},{"name":"Black-rhino tracking","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"within the crater day","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a resident population of endangered black rhino on the floor — one of East Africa''s most reliable rhino sightings, guide-radio-coordinated","si":"safari","blurb":"a resident population of endangered black rhino on the floor — one of East Africa''s most reliable rhino sightings, guide-radio-coordinated","when":"Jun-Oct  + Dec-Feb","commission":"safari DMC 10-15%"},{"name":"Olduvai Gorge - the cradle of mankind","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$30-60/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"within the Conservation Area — the human-origins site of Homo habilis and fossils to ~3.6 M years, with a museum","si":"deepdive","blurb":"within the Conservation Area — the human-origins site of Homo habilis and fossils to ~3.6 M years, with a museum","when":"Jun-Oct  + Dec-Feb","commission":"DMC/venue"},{"name":"A Maasai boma visit (highlands)","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$20-40/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the pastoralist Maasai who share the Conservation Area — a boma visit, dance and beadwork with a fair-trade operator","si":"culture","blurb":"the pastoralist Maasai who share the Conservation Area — a boma visit, dance and beadwork with a fair-trade operator","when":"Jun-Oct  + Dec-Feb","commission":"DMC/community"},{"name":"A highland crater walk (Empakaai / Olmoti)","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$60-150/pp","timing":"dry season; guided","draw_rank":1,"hook":"beyond the main crater — guided walks to the flamingo-ringed Empakaai crater lake and Olmoti''s waterfall, a rare on-foot angle in the highlands","si":"adventure","blurb":"beyond the main crater — guided walks to the flamingo-ringed Empakaai crater lake and Olmoti''s waterfall, a rare on-foot angle in the highlands","when":"dry season; guided","commission":"DMC/camp"},{"name":"A crater-rim luxury lodge honeymoon","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$1,200-3,500+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 6-12 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"&Beyond Ngorongoro Crater Lodge and the rim''s grand lodges perch on the caldera edge — fireplaces, butlers and the crater at your feet; honeymoon-grade","si":"ultra","blurb":"&Beyond Ngorongoro Crater Lodge and the rim''s grand lodges perch on the caldera edge — fireplaces, butlers and the crater at your feet; honeymoon-grade","when":"standing; peak 6-12 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC"},{"name":"Crater-rim romance (&Beyond / rim lodges)","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct  + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jun-Oct  + Dec-Feb","commission":"consortia/host"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Ngorongoro?","a":"Dangerous game and the descent, not crime. Big game is at close range on the crater floor - stay in the vehicle and follow your guide; the one-way Seneto descent drops ~600m on a steep narrow road (best in dry conditions). Carry AMREF Flying Doctors evac + travel-medical insurance for the remoteness.","source":"pangolinphoto.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Should LGBTQ+ travelers be aware of anything in Tanzania?","a":"Yes, plainly - Tanzanian law criminalizes same-sex relations and the US advisory flags targeting of LGBTQ+ travelers; a real consideration we''ll discuss candidly before booking.","source":"newsweek.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Ngorongoro Crater?","a":"Game is dense year-round (the animals don''t leave the crater), so it''s about crowds: dry Jun-Oct is best-viewing but busiest; Jan-Feb is green, quieter and pairs with the Serengeti calving; Apr-May is cheapest.","source":"asiliaafrica.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Is Ngorongoro worth it and how does it fit a trip?","a":"Yes - unmatched density and a true Big-Five day in one compact location, ideal for first-time safari-goers. It''s usually one crater day within a Northern-Circuit loop (Serengeti + Tarangire/Manyara).","source":"getsafaritours.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"What does it cost to enter Ngorongoro?","a":"The NCAA fees are significant and pass-through: ~$70.80/adult conservation entry + a $295/vehicle crater-descent fee (plus VAT), bundled into your DMC package; the safari land (lodge + game drive) is where advisor commission sits.","source":"ngorongorocratertanzania.org","si_tag":"safari"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Ngorongoro Crater Safari Guide: Big Five in a Day, Black Rhino, Fees & Best Time (Level 3)","meta_description":"Plan a Ngorongoro Crater safari - the world''s largest intact caldera (UNESCO 1979): the Big Five in a single day at Africa''s highest predator density, resident black rhino, Olduvai Gorge, Maasai highlands, 2026 NCAA fees, plus the US Level-3 advisory, timing and evac intel.","slug":"ngorongoro-crater-tanzania","primary_keyword":"Ngorongoro Crater safari","long_tail":["Ngorongoro Crater Big Five","Ngorongoro crater fees 2026","black rhino Ngorongoro","Olduvai Gorge","best time Ngorongoro","is Ngorongoro safe","Ngorongoro vs Serengeti"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Ngorongoro","Kaldera","Olduvai","faru","simba","Wamasai","Bonde la Olduvai"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-31"},"booking":{"bin":"book_with_disclosure","level":"L3","codes":["reconsider-travel","terrorism-mtwara","crime","lgbtq-targeting"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Tanzania US L3 Reconsider Travel - the terrorism concern is the Mtwara Region (far south), NOT the northern safari circuit; Ngorongoro is one of Africa''s safest/most beginner-friendly safaris with a licensed operator. Disclose L3 + confirm consent. LGBTQ+ travelers: same-sex relations criminalized + advisory flags targeting - surface plainly. Re-verify each cycle."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; SAFARI is the launch/demo SI - primary safari not globaladv; Olduvai/human-origins = deepdive; highland crater walks = globaladv; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"Olduvai Gorge / human origins"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future","note":"Maasai"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"future","note":"Empakaai/Olmoti highland walks"}],"ultra":[{"name":"&Beyond Ngorongoro Crater Lodge - the rim''s apex stay","why_ultra":"the ''Maasai Versailles'' on the caldera edge - butlered suites and the crater below","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,800-3,500+/night"},{"name":"A private crater day + Olduvai + Maasai (private guide)","why_ultra":"exclusive-vehicle Big-Five crater day + the cradle-of-mankind gorge + a Maasai boma, privately guided","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"A Northern-Circuit private-guided week (Serengeti + Ngorongoro + Tarangire)","why_ultra":"private guide/vehicle across the marquee parks, luxury camps throughout","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-31","hero":{"query":"Ngorongoro Crater, Tanzania"},"geo":{"lat":-3.2,"lng":35.5}}'::jsonb, 11),
  ('nyerere-selous-tanzania', '05A', 'Nyerere National Park (Selous)', 'Tanzania', 'A boat safari down the Rufiji, wild dogs on', 'live', 'verified', 'safariJeep', 'Tanzania — Southern Circuit / Nyerere-Selous', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","romance","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["The largest national park in Africa (~30,893 km2 - over twice the Serengeti), created 2019 from the northern part of the UNESCO-listed (1982) Selous Game Reserve, named for founding president Julius Nyerere","The Rufiji River (250+ km) makes Nyerere the finest boat-safari park in Tanzania - the signature experience (hippo, crocodile, birdlife), water-borne game viewing rare in the country","A wild-dog stronghold - one of Africa''s largest remaining African wild-dog populations (the transboundary Selous-Niassa population); the Big Five incl. a remnant black rhino (rarely seen)","US L3 Reconsider Travel - terrorism concern is the far-southern Mtwara Region near Mozambique; Nyerere''s TOURIST sector is the northern Rufiji (near Dar), away from the park''s far-southern reaches; bookable with L3 disclosure + consent; disclose LGBTQ+ targeting; licensed operator","Best Jun-Oct (dry - game on the river); green season Nov-Mar birdy/lush; long rains Apr-May close many camps; ~45-min fly-in from Dar; pair with Ruaha for a southern-circuit week","Sold via Tanzanian safari DMCs + camp consortia 10-20%+ - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; light-aircraft fly-in + TANAPA park/boat fees are pass-through; TZS (~2,633/USD, USD is the safari currency); eVisa; low wet park - malaria prophylaxis essential; AMREF for evac"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 999","hospital":"Remote low-lying river wilderness - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Dar es Salaam","advisory_level":"L3","malaria":"present and HIGHER than the northern circuit (low-elevation river park) - prophylaxis + DEET essential","yellow_fever":"not required direct from US/Europe; mandatory if transiting >12h through a risk country (e.g. Kenya)","activity_note":"L3 DISCLOSE + CONSENT (terrorism concern is the far-southern Mtwara Region near Mozambique; Nyerere''s tourist sector is the northern Rufiji, away from the far-southern reaches; disclose LGBTQ+ targeting - same-sex relations criminalized; travel with a licensed operator, keep to the northern Rufiji sector). Rufiji boat safari: keep back from hippos/crocs, life jacket, licensed crew. Walking safari only with armed ranger. Low wet park - malaria prophylaxis essential; AMREF evac","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to parts of Tanzania Tanzania FCDO advises against all but essential travel to any area within 20km of the Tanzanian border with the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, due to attacks by groups linked with Islamic extremism."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to any area within 20km of the Tanzanian border with the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, due to attacks by groups linked with Islamic extremism."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Oct (dry) - game concentrates on the Rufiji and its lakes; the premier season; book 4-8 mo ahead (few camps)","shoulder":"Nov + Jan-Mar (green flushes, good birding, softer rates/crowds)","green":"Apr-May (long rains - many camps close; roads soften)","booking_lead":"premium camps 4-8 mo for Jun-Oct (limited beds); green 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"green-season birding + boat safaris (Rufiji spectacular when full); the southern-circuit combo (Nyerere + Ruaha) as an uncrowded water-based alternative to the north","event_peaks":"Jul-Oct + Christmas/NY; the dry-season river spectacle","campaign_start":"Jun-Oct 6-9 mo out (beds scarce); the Nyerere + Ruaha southern-circuit combo by prior Aug-Oct; position as the boat-safari-and-wild-dog star beyond the northern crowds"},"jewels":[{"name":"A wild-dog stronghold + the Big Five","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"camp + park fees","timing":"Jun-Oct peak","draw_rank":1,"hook":"one of Africa''s largest remaining African wild-dog populations hunts these plains, alongside lion, leopard, elephant, buffalo and a remnant black rhino","si":"safari","blurb":"one of Africa''s largest remaining African wild-dog populations hunts these plains, alongside lion, leopard, elephant, buffalo and a remnant black rhino","when":"Jun-Oct peak","commission":"DMC/camp"},{"name":"Game drives through the largest park in Africa","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"camp + park fees","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"elephant herds, big cats and plains game across an immense, uncrowded wilderness of the Rufiji''s channels and lakes","si":"safari","blurb":"elephant herds, big cats and plains game across an immense, uncrowded wilderness of the Rufiji''s channels and lakes","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC/camp"},{"name":"The Rufiji River boat safari","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$50-150/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Nyerere''s signature — a boat drifting the wide Rufiji past hippo pods, big crocodiles and extraordinary birdlife, with elephants at the shore","si":"adventure","blurb":"Nyerere''s signature — a boat drifting the wide Rufiji past hippo pods, big crocodiles and extraordinary birdlife, with elephants at the shore","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC/camp"},{"name":"Walking safari + fly-camping","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$70-500/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Only with the armed ranger/guide, single file, downwind discipline — big-predator, big-elephant country on foot; fly-camps follow strict camp rules","si":"adventure","blurb":"Only with the armed ranger/guide, single file, downwind discipline — big-predator, big-elephant country on foot; fly-camps follow strict camp rules","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC"},{"name":"UNESCO wilderness + wild-dog conservation","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the UNESCO-listed Selous ecosystem and the Selous-Niassa wild-dog conservation story, plus the Rufiji''s ecology","si":"deepdive","blurb":"the UNESCO-listed Selous ecosystem and the Selous-Niassa wild-dog conservation story, plus the Rufiji''s ecology","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC/specialist"},{"name":"A Sand Rivers / Siwandu honeymoon","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$900-2,500+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 4-8 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Nomad''s Sand Rivers perched above the Rufiji, or Asilia''s Siwandu on a palm-fringed lake","si":"ultra","blurb":"Nomad''s Sand Rivers perched above the Rufiji, or Asilia''s Siwandu on a palm-fringed lake","when":"standing; peak 4-8 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC"},{"name":"A Rufiji riverside honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"consortia/host"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Nyerere?","a":"Not the northern Rufiji sector - the advisory''s concerns are the far-southern reaches toward the Mozambique border (terrorism, kept out of itineraries) and city petty crime, plus a flagged LGBTQ+ targeting concern travelers should weigh (Tanzanian law criminalizes same-sex relations). Practically: it''s a low-elevation river park, so malaria prophylaxis is essential, and keep back from hippos and crocs on the boat.","source":"newsweek.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What makes Nyerere different from a northern-circuit safari?","a":"The water. Alongside game drives and walking safaris, Nyerere''s signature is the Rufiji River boat safari - drifting past hippo pods, big crocodiles and extraordinary birdlife - an experience you can''t have in the Serengeti or Ngorongoro. Add one of Africa''s best wild-dog populations and near-empty wilderness, and it''s the standout of the southern circuit.","source":"nyererenationalpark.org","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Nyerere?","a":"The dry season, Jun-Oct, when game concentrates on the Rufiji and its lakes; the green season (Nov-Mar) is lush and excellent for birding, while the long rains (Apr-May) close some camps and soften the roads.","source":"expertafrica.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How do I get to Nyerere, and how long should I stay?","a":"By short fly-in from Dar (~45 min) or a 4-6-hour road transfer; give it 3-4 nights to combine boat safaris, game drives and a walking safari - ideally paired with Ruaha for a full southern-circuit week.","source":"expertafrica.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Tanzania?","a":"eVisa required - apply on the official portal before departure. Yellow fever is not required direct from the US/Europe, but is mandatory if you transit >12 h through a risk country like Kenya.","source":"tanzania-specialist.com","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Nyerere National Park (Selous) Guide: Rufiji Boat Safaris, Wild Dogs & Best Time","meta_description":"Plan a Nyerere/Selous safari - the largest national park in Africa: the Rufiji River boat safari, one of Africa''s best wild-dog populations, the Big Five and near-empty UNESCO wilderness - with the US Level-3 advisory, best time (Jun-Oct), the fly-in from Dar and where to stay on the southern circuit.","slug":"nyerere-selous-tanzania","primary_keyword":"Nyerere National Park Selous safari","long_tail":["Rufiji River boat safari","Selous wild dogs","Nyerere National Park boat safari","Selous vs Serengeti","is Tanzania safe safari","Nyerere best time to visit","southern circuit Tanzania"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Nyerere","Selous","Rufiji","mbwa mwitu","kiboko","mto"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-01"},"booking":{"bin":"book_with_disclosure","level":"L3","codes":["reconsider-travel","mtwara-mozambique-border-carveout-far","lgbtq-targeting"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Tanzania US L3 Reconsider Travel - the terrorism concern is the Mtwara Region (far southern coast near Mozambique). Nyerere''s photographic TOURIST sector is the northern Rufiji (near Dar), away from the park''s far-southern reaches toward the Mozambique border. Bookable with L3 disclosure + consent; also disclose the LGBTQ+ targeting consideration (same-sex relations criminalized). Travel with a licensed operator; keep to the northern Rufiji sector. Re-verify each cycle."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":6,"misses":16,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; per the safari-build rule big game/wild dogs is safari (PRIMARY here), NOT globaladv; the Rufiji boat safari + walking + fly-camping = globaladv; river (cruise) is a documented MISS - a safari boat, not a river-cruise ship; UNESCO/wild-dog conservation/Rufiji ecology = deepdive; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"big-game/wild dogs - a wild-dog stronghold + the Big Five (PRIMARY)"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"Rufiji River boat safari (signature) + walking safari + fly-camping"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"Sand Rivers Selous / Siwandu"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"UNESCO / wild-dog conservation / Rufiji ecology"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Sand Rivers Selous (Nomad) / Siwandu (Asilia) - the riverside-luxury apex","why_ultra":"a stone lodge above the Rufiji and a lakeside tented camp, deep in Africa''s largest park, with private boat safaris and walking","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,200-2,500+/night"},{"name":"A private boat-and-wild-dog week","why_ultra":"an exclusive-guide safari: Rufiji boat safaris + wild-dog tracking + walking + a fly-camp night, from an ultra camp","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"The private southern-circuit safari (Nyerere + Ruaha)","why_ultra":"Tanzania''s wild south flown and privately guided: Nyerere''s Rufiji boats + Ruaha''s great lion prides, far from the northern crowds","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Nyerere National Park (Selous), Tanzania"},"geo":{"lat":-8,"lng":37.6}}'::jsonb, 12),
  ('nyungwe-forest-rwanda', '05A', 'Nyungwe Forest National Park', 'Rwanda', 'An ancient cloud forest', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Rwanda — Nyungwe Forest', '{"adventure","ultra","romance","deepdive","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Rwanda''s ancient montane rainforest (~1,019 km2) on the Congo-Nile divide (Nile headwaters) - 13 primate species incl. 500+ chimpanzees and one of East Africa''s biggest colobus troops (up to ~400)","The chimp trek is the draw (globaladv-primary) - a strenuous 2-6h hike to a 1-hour habituated encounter, $250 permit (vs Rwanda''s $1,500 gorilla permit); safari (big-game) is a MISS - a forest, not a Big-Five park","East Africa''s FIRST canopy walkway (160m long, 70m high; $60); the Isumo waterfall hike (~10.6km, 4-5h, $15); 300+ birds incl. 29 Albertine-Rift endemics - a birder''s grail","US L3 Reconsider Travel (2026 regional Ebola-alert; was L2) - Nyungwe is SW Rwanda (Burundi side), away from the 10km DRC-border L4 carve-out; disclose L3 + consent","Best Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb (hiking/canopy, firmer trails); chimps often best Oct-May (fruiting); pairs into the 3-park Rwanda circuit with Volcanoes (gorillas) + Akagera (Big Five)","Sold via Rwandan safari DMCs 10-20% - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; the $250 RDB chimp permit + canopy ($60)/waterfall ($15) fees are pass-through; RWF (~1,467/USD); visa on arrival $30; malaria present (lower at altitude); AMREF for evac"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (police) / 912 ambulance / 111 fire; AMREF Flying Doctors for high-forest evac","hospital":"Remote/high forest - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Huye/Kigali","advisory_level":"L3","malaria":"present (chloroquine-resistant) - prophylaxis advised (lower at Nyungwe''s 1,600-2,950m but real); DEET","yellow_fever":"required only if arriving from a YF-endemic country (not direct from the US)","activity_note":"L3 DISCLOSE + CONSENT (2026 regional Ebola-alert; Nyungwe is SW Rwanda, away from the DRC-border L4 carve-out). Chimp trek = strenuous 2-6h over steep/slippery montane slopes (good boots + fitness), rules 7-8m/mask/1hr/armed ranger. Canopy walkway sways 70m up (head-for-heights). Remote - carry AMREF evac + insurance","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Rusizi District FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the parts of Rusizi District which are within 10km of the border with the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC), including the Rwandan islands in Lake Kivu and Kamembe Airport."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to parts of the Rubavu and Rusizi Districts."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/rwanda","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-06-10T15:14:19+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb (drier, firmer trails) for canopy walk/hiking/primates","shoulder":"Oct-Nov + Mar (softer rates; often better for chimps - fruiting)","green":"Apr-May (long rains - lush, muddiest, cheapest; chimps can be closer)","booking_lead":"lodges (very few) 2-5 mo for Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb; green 1-2 mo","off_season_specials":"the 3-park Rwanda circuit (Volcanoes + Nyungwe + Akagera) unlocks the Nov-May 30% gorilla-permit discount - sell Nyungwe as the forest/chimp leg; wet-season chimp + birding value","event_peaks":"Jun-Sep + Christmas/NY; birding season (migrants)","campaign_start":"Jun-Sep hiking/canopy 4-6 mo out; 3-park circuit (with the gorilla discount) by prior Aug-Sep; position as the active affordable primate day beside the gorillas"},"jewels":[{"name":"Chimpanzee trekking","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$250 permit + land","timing":"year-round; chimps best Oct-May","draw_rank":1,"hook":"A one-hour habituated-chimp encounter for a $250 permit — a strenuous, thrilling forest trek","si":"adventure","blurb":"A one-hour habituated-chimp encounter for a $250 permit — a strenuous, thrilling forest trek","when":"year-round; chimps best Oct-May","commission":"DMC/RDB"},{"name":"East Africa''s first canopy walkway","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$60/pp","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"A 160-m suspension bridge, 70 m above the forest floor — the region''s first — for $60","si":"adventure","blurb":"A 160-m suspension bridge, 70 m above the forest floor — the region''s first — for $60","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","commission":"DMC/RDB"},{"name":"Colobus trekking + the Isumo waterfall hike","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$15-90/pp","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","draw_rank":3,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"track a colobus troop up to 400 strong through the canopy, and hike the ~10.6-km Isumo waterfall trail — the accessible, budget-friendly forest days","si":"adventure","blurb":"track a colobus troop up to 400 strong through the canopy, and hike the ~10.6-km Isumo waterfall trail — the accessible, budget-friendly forest days","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","commission":"DMC/RDB"},{"name":"Albertine-Rift birding + biodiversity","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"300+ birds with 29 Albertine-Rift endemics and 13 primate species on the Congo–Nile divide","si":"deepdive","blurb":"300+ birds with 29 Albertine-Rift endemics and 13 primate species on the Congo–Nile divide","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","commission":"DMC/specialist"},{"name":"A One&Only Nyungwe House honeymoon","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$1,000-3,000+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 2-5 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"a tea-estate-set forest retreat — glass-walled suites over the canopy, a spa, private guiding and the forest at the door","si":"ultra","blurb":"a tea-estate-set forest retreat — glass-walled suites over the canopy, a spa, private guiding and the forest at the door","when":"standing; peak 2-5 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC"},{"name":"A tea-estate + forest-wellness day","si_tag":"culture","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$20-80/pp","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the emerald tea plantations that ring Nyungwe, a plucking-and-tasting visit, and the forest''s own serenity — a gentle, restorative counterpoint to the trekking","si":"culture","blurb":"the emerald tea plantations that ring Nyungwe, a plucking-and-tasting visit, and the forest''s own serenity — a gentle, restorative counterpoint to the trekking","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","commission":"DMC/community"},{"name":"A Nyungwe forest honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a tea-estate-set forest retreat — glass-walled suites over the canopy, a spa, private guiding and the forest at the door","si":"romance","blurb":"a tea-estate-set forest retreat — glass-walled suites over the canopy, a spa, private guiding and the forest at the door","when":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb  for canopy walk/hiking/primates","commission":"consortia/host"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Nyungwe?","a":"The trek and the health advisory - not crime. Chimp trekking is a strenuous 2-6-hour hike over steep, slippery montane slopes (good boots + fitness), and the canopy walkway sways 70 m up (a head-for-heights helps). Malaria is present (prophylaxis + DEET, lower at altitude), and it''s remote - carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How much is chimp trekking, and how does it compare to gorillas?","a":"The chimp permit is $250 (vs Rwanda''s $1,500 gorilla permit) - a more affordable, more active primate trek: faster-moving chimps, a 2-6-hour hike, a one-hour encounter (7-8 m distance, a face mask, an armed ranger). It pairs beautifully with the gorillas of Volcanoes.","source":"greatadventuresafaris.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"What else is there besides chimps at Nyungwe?","a":"Plenty: the canopy walk ($60), huge colobus troops (up to 400), the Isumo waterfall hike ($15), world-class birding (29 Albertine-Rift endemics), and tea plantations on the forest edge - Nyungwe rewards a 2-3-day stay.","source":"nyungweforestnationalpark.org","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Nyungwe?","a":"For hiking, the canopy walk and general primates, come in the drier Jun-Sep and Dec-Feb (firmer trails); for chimp trekking, the wetter Oct-May can be better (abundant fruit keeps chimps lower and closer).","source":"safaris-uganda.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Rwanda?","a":"Visa on arrival $30 (or online via Irembo); passport valid 6 months. Yellow fever is required only if arriving from a YF-endemic country (not direct from the US).","source":"thingstodoinrwanda.com","si_tag":"globaladv"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Nyungwe Forest Guide: Chimpanzee Trekking, the Canopy Walk, Permits & Best Time","meta_description":"Plan a Nyungwe Forest trip - Rwanda''s ancient montane rainforest: chimpanzee trekking ($250), East Africa''s first canopy walkway (70 m up), colobus troops up to 400, the Isumo waterfall hike and world-class Albertine-Rift birding - with the US Level-3 advisory, fitness and cost, and the 3-park Rwanda circuit.","slug":"nyungwe-forest-rwanda","primary_keyword":"Nyungwe Forest chimpanzee trekking","long_tail":["Nyungwe chimpanzee permit cost 2026","Nyungwe canopy walk","colobus monkeys Nyungwe","Nyungwe waterfall hike","Nyungwe vs Volcanoes","is Nyungwe safe","Nyungwe birding Albertine Rift"],"search_language":"fr","local_keywords":["Nyungwe","inguge","canopy walk","colobus","Isumo","Gisakura","Albertine Rift"],"hreflang":["en","fr"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-01"},"booking":{"bin":"book_with_disclosure","level":"L3","codes":["reconsider-travel","regional-ebola-alert"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Rwanda US L3 Reconsider Travel (2026 regional Ebola-alert precaution; was L2). Nyungwe is SW Rwanda (Burundi side), away from the 10km DRC-border L4 carve-out (which applies to Volcanoes/NW). Disclose L3 + confirm consent. Re-verify each cycle."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; per the safari-build rule the chimp trek is globaladv (PRIMARY here) - safari (big-game) is a documented MISS on a montane forest; canopy walk + waterfall hikes = globaladv; birding/biodiversity = deepdive; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"chimp trekking + canopy walk + colobus + waterfall hikes (PRIMARY)"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"One&Only Nyungwe House"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"Albertine-Rift biodiversity / birding"},{"si":"culture","name":"culture","status":"future","note":"tea communities"}],"ultra":[{"name":"One&Only Nyungwe House - the forest''s apex stay","why_ultra":"glass-walled suites on a tea estate at the forest edge, a spa, and private guiding to the chimps + canopy walk","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,500-3,000+/night"},{"name":"A private chimp + canopy + colobus + birding week","why_ultra":"an exclusive-guide forest immersion: two chimp treks, the canopy walk, colobus, the waterfall hike + specialist birding, from an ultra lodge","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"The 3-park luxury Rwanda circuit (Volcanoes + Nyungwe + Akagera)","why_ultra":"gorillas + chimps/canopy walk + the Big-Five savanna, private-guided - and it unlocks the Nov-May 30% gorilla-permit discount","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Nyungwe Forest National Park, Rwanda"},"geo":{"lat":-2.5,"lng":29.2}}'::jsonb, 13),
  ('queen-elizabeth-np-uganda', '05A', 'Queen Elizabeth National Park', 'Uganda', 'Tree-climbing lions, a hippo-thronged channel and 600 birds', 'future', 'verified', 'lion', 'Uganda — Queen Elizabeth / Rift Valley', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["BOOKING HOLD: Uganda US L4 Do Not Travel driven by an Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. CONTENT-ONLY, no Book path, no waiver. DYNAMIC - re-verify each cycle, flip to live when it clears. Redirect safari demand to Kenya/Tanzania/Akagera","Uganda''s most popular savanna park (~1,978 km2, est. 1952 as Kazinga NP, renamed for Queen Elizabeth II): 95+ mammals and 600+ birds - the country''s most biodiverse safari","The tree-climbing lions of Ishasha (lions in fig/acacia trees - rare behaviour); the Kazinga Channel (40km, Lakes Edward<->George; UWA boat $30 - hippos/crocs/elephants/birds); Kyambura Gorge chimps","Western edge borders Virunga (DR Congo) - a separate STANDING security concern even apart from the Ebola L4","Park fee $40 (24h); yellow fever MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe); eVisa (no visa-on-arrival); malaria in all regions (prophylaxis)","Live twins = Kenya (Maasai Mara/Amboseli L2), Tanzania (Serengeti L3), akagera-np-rwanda (Rwanda Big Five L3). Anchors the Uganda cluster with bwindi/murchison-falls/kibale"],"safety":{"emergency":"999 / 112","hospital":"Remote - AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance; nearest referral Kasese/Mbarara/Kampala","malaria":"present in all regions - prophylaxis","yellow_fever":"MANDATORY for entry (all >=1yr, checked at Entebbe, >=10 days before)","ebola":"Sudan virus outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. Health information, not an advisory against travel - the FCDO restricts nothing in Uganda; re-verify current outbreak status before travel","drc_border":"western edge borders Virunga (DR Congo) - separate standing security concern; when live, keep to eastern/central sectors","activity_note":"Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak is standing health information to re-verify each cycle - not a booking hold (health-based holds released, David 2026-08-29). The DRC border is a separate standing security note (see drc_border). Standard game-drive/boat rules, keep back from hippos/crocs, ranger-guided","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the DRC provinces that border Uganda."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to these DRC provinces."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to the provinces of DRC that border Uganda, including Virunga National Park."},{"form":"against all travel","text":"advises against all travel to South Sudan."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-27T15:00:28+01:00"}},"timing":{"booking_status":"HELD - no live demand capture while Level 4 stands (no campaigns/fire-dates)","latent_peak":"Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb (drier - game at water, firmer tracks) - IF cleared","latent_green":"Mar-May + Oct-Nov (rains, lush/birdy, softer rates)","latent_booking_lead":"lodges 2-4 mo peak - NOT applicable while held","reverify_trigger":"check Uganda''s advisory EVERY publish cycle - DYNAMIC health advisory; flip to live the moment it drops below L4; re-verify western DRC/Virunga line before live routing","redirect":"live safari demand -> Kenya (Maasai Mara/Amboseli L2) / Tanzania (Serengeti L3) / akagera-np-rwanda (Rwanda Big Five L3)"},"jewels":[{"name":"The tree-climbing lions of Ishasha","si_tag":"safari","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD; latent Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","draw_rank":null,"hook":"one of only a couple of places on Earth where lions habitually lounge in fig and acacia trees","si":"safari","blurb":"one of only a couple of places on Earth where lions habitually lounge in fig and acacia trees","when":"HELD; latent Jun-Sep + Dec-Feb","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"The Kazinga Channel boat cruise","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"held","tier":"essential","price_band":"HELD (UWA boat $30 latent)","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"a 40-km natural channel between Lakes Edward and George","si":"adventure","blurb":"a 40-km natural channel between Lakes Edward and George","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"Kyambura Gorge chimpanzee trek","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"a sunken \"valley of apes\" — a forested gorge in the savanna holding a habituated chimp community; a globaladv trek unique to Queen Elizabeth","si":"adventure","blurb":"a sunken \"valley of apes\" — a forested gorge in the savanna holding a habituated chimp community; a globaladv trek unique to Queen Elizabeth","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"A 600-bird birder''s grail","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"held","tier":"premier","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"Uganda''s most bird-rich park — 600+ species across savanna, wetland, forest and lake habitats, from shoebill-country wetlands to Kazinga''s pelicans and skimmers","si":"deepdive","blurb":"Uganda''s most bird-rich park — 600+ species across savanna, wetland, forest and lake habitats, from shoebill-country wetlands to Kazinga''s pelicans and skimmers","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"},{"name":"A Rift-Valley safari-lodge honeymoon (held)","si_tag":"ultra","status":"held","tier":"comfort","price_band":"HELD - no book path","timing":"HELD","draw_rank":null,"hook":"Mweya Safari Lodge on its channel-side peninsula, Ishasha Wilderness Camp, Kyambura Gorge Lodge — crater-lake and channel luxury after the game drive","si":"ultra","blurb":"Mweya Safari Lodge on its channel-side peninsula, Ishasha Wilderness Camp, Kyambura Gorge Lodge — crater-lake and channel luxury after the game drive","when":"HELD","commission":"none (advisory hold)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Where can I go on safari instead, right now?","a":"Kenya (Maasai Mara / Amboseli, US L2, bookable) or Tanzania (Serengeti / Ngorongoro, US L3, bookable) for the classic Big-game plains - or Akagera, Rwanda (US L3, a Big-Five comeback ~2h from Kigali) for the nearest live savanna. We route all Uganda safari demand there.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Will this clear - should I wait for Queen Elizabeth?","a":"Possibly - this is a health-driven, dynamic advisory (an outbreak, not conflict), so it can be lifted when the outbreak is contained. We re-verify Uganda''s status every publish cycle and will flip the park to bookable the moment it drops below Level 4. For a firm 2026 safari, book Kenya, Tanzania or Akagera now.","source":"travelweekly.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What would Queen Elizabeth offer when it reopens?","a":"Uganda''s most popular savanna - the tree-climbing lions of Ishasha, the Kazinga Channel boat cruise (hippos, crocs, elephants, 600+ birds), Kyambura Gorge chimps, and a Rift-Valley backdrop of crater lakes. All held until the advisory lifts.","source":"ugandawildlife.org","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Is the DRC border a concern too?","a":"Yes - separately. The park''s western edge borders Virunga in the DR Congo, a standing security concern in its own right; when the park is live, itineraries keep to the eastern/central sectors. **FCDO travel advice for Uganda:** the FCDO names no advisory against travel to Uganda. *https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uganda — page updated 2026-07-27.*","source":"national-parks.org","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are the non-Ebola health requirements for Uganda?","a":"Yellow fever is mandatory for entry (all travelers >=1 yr, checked at Entebbe, vaccinate >=10 days before); malaria prophylaxis is essential (all regions); carry AMREF Flying Doctors + insurance. All moot while the L4 hold stands.","source":"cdc.gov","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Queen Elizabeth NP, Uganda: Tree-Climbing Lions & the Kazinga Channel - On Hold (Level 4 / Ebola)","meta_description":"Queen Elizabeth National Park - Uganda''s most popular savanna: the tree-climbing lions of Ishasha, the Kazinga Channel boat cruise, Kyambura Gorge chimps and 600+ birds - is currently a US Level 4 ''Do Not Travel'' zone (Ebola outbreak). What it is, why it''s held, and where to safari instead (Kenya, Tanzania, Rwanda''s Akagera).","slug":"queen-elizabeth-np-uganda","primary_keyword":"Queen Elizabeth National Park tree-climbing lions","long_tail":["Kazinga Channel boat cruise","Ishasha tree-climbing lions","Kyambura Gorge chimps","is Uganda safe Ebola","Queen Elizabeth vs Maasai Mara","Queen Elizabeth NP birds"],"search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Queen Elizabeth","Kazinga","Ishasha","Kyambura","empologoma","Mweya"],"hreflang":["en"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-01"},"booking":{"bin":"booking_hold","level":"L4","codes":["do-not-travel","ebola-sudan-virus-pheic","health-outbreak","drc-border-adjacent"],"book_suppressed":true,"waiver":false,"dynamic":true,"note":"Uganda US L4 Do Not Travel driven by an Ebola (Sudan virus) outbreak - PHEIC declared 2026-05-17. CONTENT-ONLY, Book button suppressed, no waiver. DYNAMIC health advisory - re-verify EVERY publish cycle; flip to live the moment it drops below L4. Separately note the western DRC/Virunga border (standing security concern). Redirect live safari demand to Kenya (Maasai Mara/Amboseli L2), Tanzania (Serengeti L3), akagera-np-rwanda (Rwanda Big Five L3)."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":6,"misses":16,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; EVERY hit is HELD behind the L4 booking hold - no SI is servable while Level 4 stands; safari = Big-game + tree-climbing lions (primary when live), globaladv = Kazinga boat + Kyambura chimp trek; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"held","note":"Big-game + tree-climbing lions of Ishasha"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"held","note":"Kazinga Channel boat + Kyambura Gorge chimps"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"held"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"held","note":"600+ birds - birder''s grail"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Kyambura Gorge Lodge / Mweya Safari Lodge (HELD)","why_ultra":"the park''s apex stays - a converted coffee store above the chimp gorge and a channel-side peninsula lodge; documented for the day the hold lifts, sold by no one today","earning":"none while held","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"n/a (L4 booking hold)","tier":"ultra","status":"HELD"},{"name":"A private Ishasha + Kazinga + Kyambura week (HELD)","why_ultra":"tree-climbing lions + the channel boat + the chimp gorge + the crater lakes, privately guided - latent","earning":"none while held","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"n/a (L4 booking hold)","tier":"ultra","status":"HELD"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Queen Elizabeth National Park, Uganda"},"geo":{"lat":-0.2,"lng":30}}'::jsonb, 14),
  ('ruaha-tanzania', '05A', 'Ruaha National Park', 'Tanzania', 'One in ten of the world''s lions, wild dogs', 'live', 'verified', 'lion', 'Tanzania — Southern Circuit / Ruaha', '{"safari","adventure","ultra","romance","deepdive"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Tanzania''s largest national park (~20,226 km2) and a global lion stronghold - an estimated ~10% of the world''s lions, in some of the largest prides ever recorded (hunt buffalo and even giraffe)","One of East Africa''s best wild-dog destinations - within the 3rd-largest wild-dog population in the world; ~12,000 elephants in the greater ecosystem; a rare East-meets-Southern-Africa transition zone (greater + lesser kudu, sable, roan)","The Great Ruaha River is the dry-season lifeline and focus of game viewing; 570+ birds; remote, uncrowded, mainly fly-in (south-central Tanzania, ~130 km west of Iringa)","US L3 Reconsider Travel - terrorism concern is the Mtwara Region (far southeastern coast, well away); bookable with L3 disclosure + consent; disclose LGBTQ+ targeting; travel with a licensed operator","Best Jun-Oct (dry - game on the river); green season Nov-Apr lush/birdy (some camps close); Ruaha''s signature is the walking safari (+ night drives + fly-camping); no rhino (poached out - four of Big Five)","Sold via Tanzanian safari DMCs + camp consortia 10-20%+ - IATAN/host-gated, CLIA has NO Africa representation; light-aircraft fly-in + TANAPA park fees are pass-through; TZS (~2,633/USD, USD is the safari currency); eVisa; AMREF evac essential (remote interior)"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 / 999","hospital":"Remote deep-interior - medical access by air; AMREF Flying Doctors (~$40 pp/30d) + travel-medical insurance essential; nearest referral Iringa/Dar","advisory_level":"L3","malaria":"present (interior park) - prophylaxis + DEET advised","yellow_fever":"not required direct from US/Europe; mandatory if transiting >12h through a risk country (e.g. Kenya)","activity_note":"L3 DISCLOSE + CONSENT (terrorism concern is the far-southeastern Mtwara Region, well away; disclose LGBTQ+ targeting - same-sex relations criminalized; travel with a licensed operator). Ruaha is a remote fly-in wilderness - AMREF evac + insurance are load-bearing. Walking safari only with armed ranger (single file, downwind, no bright colors); predator-dense driving (keep still/quiet, never on foot near a kill); night drives to vehicle rules","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to parts of Tanzania Tanzania FCDO advises against all but essential travel to any area within 20km of the Tanzanian border with the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, due to attacks by groups linked with Islamic extremism."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to any area within 20km of the Tanzanian border with the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, due to attacks by groups linked with Islamic extremism."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Jun-Oct (dry) - game concentrates on the Great Ruaha River; the premier predator season; book 4-8 mo ahead (few camps)","shoulder":"Nov + late Oct (good rates, softer crowds)","green":"Dec-Apr (rains - lush, superb birding, cheapest; some camps close, roads soften)","booking_lead":"premium camps 4-8 mo for Jun-Oct (limited beds); green 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"green-season birding + big-cat cubs (Dec-Apr); the southern-circuit combo (Ruaha + Nyerere/Selous) as an uncrowded alternative to the north","event_peaks":"Jul-Oct + Christmas/NY; the dry-season predator spectacle","campaign_start":"Jun-Oct 6-9 mo out (beds scarce); the Ruaha + Nyerere southern-circuit combo by prior Aug-Oct; position as the connoisseur''s uncrowded predator safari for northern-circuit returnees"},"jewels":[{"name":"The lion kingdom","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"camp + park fees","timing":"Jun-Oct peak","draw_rank":1,"hook":"an estimated one in ten of the world''s lions live in Ruaha, in some of the largest prides ever recorded","si":"safari","blurb":"an estimated one in ten of the world''s lions live in Ruaha, in some of the largest prides ever recorded","when":"Jun-Oct peak","commission":"DMC/camp"},{"name":"Wild dogs + a transition-zone roster","si_tag":"safari","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"camp + park fees","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"one of the world''s best wild-dog strongholds, plus a rare East-meets-Southern-Africa game list — greater and lesser kudu, sable, roan","si":"safari","blurb":"one of the world''s best wild-dog strongholds, plus a rare East-meets-Southern-Africa game list — greater and lesser kudu, sable, roan","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC/camp"},{"name":"Walking safari + fly-camping + night drives","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$60-500/pp","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Ruaha is one of Tanzania''s great walking-safari parks","si":"adventure","blurb":"Ruaha is one of Tanzania''s great walking-safari parks","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC"},{"name":"Predator research + transition-zone biodiversity","si_tag":"deepdive","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Ruaha is a hub of lion and wild-dog conservation science in a globally significant ecosystem, plus a 570-bird list","si":"deepdive","blurb":"Ruaha is a hub of lion and wild-dog conservation science in a globally significant ecosystem, plus a 570-bird list","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC/specialist"},{"name":"A Jabali Ridge / Mwagusi honeymoon","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$900-2,500+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 4-8 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Asilia''s Jabali Ridge tucked into a kopje above the plains, or Mwagusi''s legendary bush bandas on a sand river","si":"ultra","blurb":"Asilia''s Jabali Ridge tucked into a kopje above the plains, or Mwagusi''s legendary bush bandas on a sand river","when":"standing; peak 4-8 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC"},{"name":"A Ruaha wilderness honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"consortia/host"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Ruaha?","a":"Not the parks - the advisory''s concerns are the far-southeastern Mtwara Region (terrorism, far away) and city petty crime, plus a flagged LGBTQ+ targeting concern travelers should weigh (Tanzanian law criminalizes same-sex relations). In Ruaha itself the risks are ordinary safari ones plus remoteness - it''s a fly-in wilderness, so carry AMREF evac + insurance and follow the walking-safari rules.","source":"newsweek.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Why choose Ruaha over the northern circuit?","a":"For wildness and predators without the crowds - ~10% of the world''s lions in huge prides, one of the world''s best wild-dog populations, big elephant herds and a transition-zone game roster, all in Tanzania''s largest park with a fraction of the vehicles. It''s the connoisseur''s safari, best paired with Nyerere/Selous.","source":"national-parks.org","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Ruaha?","a":"The dry season, Jun-Oct, when the Great Ruaha River becomes the only water and game - lions, dogs, elephants - concentrates dramatically along it; the green season (Nov-Apr) is lush and superb for birds (570+ species) but some camps close and roads soften.","source":"getsafaritours.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How do I get to Ruaha, and how long should I stay?","a":"Mostly by light-aircraft fly-in (from Dar, Iringa or as part of a southern-circuit hop); give it 3-4 nights to justify the flight and to do the river drives and a walking safari - it''s not a day-trip park.","source":"getsafaritours.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Tanzania?","a":"eVisa required - apply on the official portal before departure. Yellow fever is not required direct from the US/Europe, but is mandatory if you transit >12 h through a risk country like Kenya.","source":"tanzania-specialist.com","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Ruaha National Park Guide: Lions, Wild Dogs, Walking Safaris & Best Time","meta_description":"Plan a Ruaha safari - Tanzania''s largest, wildest and least-crowded park: ~10% of the world''s lions in record prides, one of the world''s best wild-dog populations, walking safaris and the Great Ruaha River - with the US Level-3 advisory, best time (Jun-Oct), the fly-in and where to stay on the southern circuit.","slug":"ruaha-tanzania","primary_keyword":"Ruaha National Park safari","long_tail":["Ruaha lions prides","Ruaha wild dogs","Ruaha walking safari","Ruaha vs Serengeti","is Tanzania safe safari","Ruaha best time to visit","southern circuit Tanzania"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Ruaha","simba","mbwa mwitu","tembo","mto"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-01"},"booking":{"bin":"book_with_disclosure","level":"L3","codes":["reconsider-travel","mtwara-terrorism-carveout-far","lgbtq-targeting"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"Tanzania US L3 Reconsider Travel - the terrorism concern is the Mtwara Region (far southeastern coast), well away from Ruaha in the south-central interior. Bookable with L3 disclosure + consent; also disclose the LGBTQ+ targeting consideration (same-sex relations criminalized). Travel with a licensed operator; remote fly-in - AMREF evac essential. Re-verify each cycle."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":6,"misses":16,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; per the safari-build rule big game/predators is safari (PRIMARY here - lion + wild-dog stronghold), NOT globaladv; walking safari + night drive + fly-camping = globaladv; predator research + transition-zone biodiversity + 570 birds = deepdive; no rhino - poached out (four of Big Five); sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"safari","name":"safari","status":"live","note":"big-game/predators - ~10% of the world''s lions + a wild-dog stronghold (PRIMARY)"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live","note":"walking safari + night drive + fly-camping"},{"si":"ultra","name":"ultra","status":"live","note":"Jabali Ridge / Mwagusi"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"live"},{"si":"deepdive","name":"deepdive","status":"future","note":"predator research / transition-zone biodiversity / 570 birds"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Jabali Ridge (Asilia) / Mwagusi - the wilderness-luxury apex","why_ultra":"a kopje-set design lodge and a legendary sand-river camp, deep in Tanzania''s largest park, with walking safaris and private guiding","earning":"consortia/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":true,"mor":"commissionable-rack","tier":"ultra","price_band":"~$1,200-2,500+/night"},{"name":"A private lion-and-wild-dog walking week","why_ultra":"an exclusive-guide safari: river drives for the great prides + walking safaris + a fly-camp night + wild-dog tracking, from an ultra camp","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"},{"name":"The private southern-circuit safari (Ruaha + Nyerere/Selous)","why_ultra":"Tanzania''s wild south flown and privately guided: Ruaha''s predators + Nyerere''s Rufiji boat safaris, far from the northern crowds","earning":"DMC/consortia","virtuoso_value_add":false,"mor":"commissionable","tier":"ultra","price_band":"on application"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-01","hero":{"query":"Ruaha National Park, Tanzania"},"geo":{"lat":-7.7,"lng":34.8333}}'::jsonb, 15)
